00:17:08,111 --> 00:17:10,071
Where did you find an Iron Giant?

233
00:17:10,238 --> 00:17:12,908
AECH: Find it? I'm building it.
That's a commission.

234
00:17:13,116 --> 00:17:15,911
WADE: Oh, yeah. Aech is top-rated
on the mod boards.

235
00:17:16,077 --> 00:17:18,747
People all over the OASIS
pay him serious coin.

236
00:17:18,914 --> 00:17:21,124
Oh, hey, check this out!

237
00:17:21,291 --> 00:17:22,751
AECH: Hey. Z, yo.

238
00:17:24,294 --> 00:17:26,588
- The <i>Galactica,</i> of course.
- These are my babies, all right, man?

239
00:17:26,755 --> 00:17:28,381
<i>Sulaco,</i> from <i>Aliens.</i>

240
00:17:28,548 --> 00:17:29,925
Dude, how are you showing off my shit?

241
00:17:30,091 --> 00:17:32,552
<i>Valley Forge,</i> from <i>Silent Running.</i>
Oh, where's the Harkonnen Drop-Ship?

242
00:17:32,719 --> 00:17:35,096
That thing is sick.
Folds space like a boss.

243
00:17:35,263 --> 00:17:37,015
I mean, you can get from Incipio
to Arrakis in three seconds...

244
00:17:37,349 --> 00:17:38,934
Fingers!

245
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,268
You'll have to excuse him.

246
00:17:40,435 --> 00:17:42,604
He gets a little nervous
around pretty girls.

247
00:17:42,687 --> 00:17:44,105
(SNAPS FINGERS)

248
00:17:48,026 --> 00:17:49,236
(BEEPING)

249
00:17:49,778 --> 00:17:52,239
I can fix it in 10 minutes.

250
00:17:53,615 --> 00:17:56,076
Yup. He's pretty great.

251
00:17:56,243 --> 00:17:59,120
I assume you and Shoulder Blades
are clanned up.

252
00:17:59,287 --> 00:18:01,414
Oh, Aech? Nah.

253
00:18:01,581 --> 00:18:05,710
I mean, he's really good,
but I don't clan.

254
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:09,089
Oh, 'cause you're Parzival,

255
00:18:09,256 --> 00:18:11,633
as in the knight
who found the Holy Grail by himself.

256
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,385
What about you, Art3mis?

257
00:18:13,551 --> 00:18:16,763
Goddess of the hunt.
Clans must be killing to sign you up.

258
00:18:18,390 --> 00:18:20,183
- Favorite shooter?
- Excuse me?

259
00:18:20,350 --> 00:18:22,143
James Halliday's
favorite first-person shooter.

260
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:23,728
- What?
- Oh. <i>GoldenEye.</i>

261
00:18:23,895 --> 00:18:26,106
- Playing as?
- Oddjob. Is this a test?

262
00:18:26,273 --> 00:18:27,274
Favorite game variant?

263
00:18:27,357 --> 00:18:28,942
Game variant was "slappers only."
No weapons.

264
00:18:29,109 --> 00:18:31,111
I know what "slappers only" means.
Racer?

265
00:18:31,278 --> 00:18:33,405
<i>Turbo.</i> And his favorite food
was Hot Pockets.

266
00:18:33,571 --> 00:18:35,156
Favorite restaurant was Chuck E Cheese.

267
00:18:35,323 --> 00:18:37,701
Song was <i>Video Killed the Radio Star</i>
by the Buggles.

268
00:18:37,867 --> 00:18:39,494
Video was <i>Take on Me</i> by A-ha.

269
00:18:39,786 --> 00:18:43,707
Oh, oh...
His favorite quote was from <i>Superman.</i>

270
00:18:44,374 --> 00:18:45,667
"Some people can read <i>War and Peace</i>

271
00:18:45,834 --> 00:18:48,044
"and come away thinking
it's a simple adventure story..."

272
00:18:48,211 --> 00:18:50,839
"Others can read the ingredients
on the back of a chewing-gum wrapper

273
00:18:51,006 --> 00:18:53,383
"and unlock
the secrets of the universe."

274
00:18:54,092 --> 00:18:56,094
Lex Luthor. (CHUCKLES)

275
00:18:56,511 --> 00:18:58,013
Cool.

276
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:03,059
What would you do? If you won.
The whole contest, I mean.

277
00:19:03,143 --> 00:19:06,062
Oh! I mean, I've got tons of plans
in the real world.

278
00:19:06,229 --> 00:19:10,984
I'd move into a huge mansion,
buy a bunch of cool shit, not be poor.

279
00:19:12,235 --> 00:19:14,612
Now I know why you stopped short.

280
00:19:15,947 --> 00:19:18,950
I stopped because of Kong.
No one ever makes it past Kong.

281
00:19:19,117 --> 00:19:20,910
That's, like, a rule.

282
00:19:21,077 --> 00:19:24,539
Well, then you know it can't be true.
Because Halliday hated making rules.

283
00:19:24,706 --> 00:19:25,999
I can't afford to zero out.

284
00:19:26,166 --> 00:19:27,542
- You're afraid to lose your shit.
- No, I'm not!

285
00:19:27,709 --> 00:19:29,669
What happens
when IOI offers you guaranteed coin

286
00:19:29,836 --> 00:19:31,004
for the keys to the kingdom?

287
00:19:31,171 --> 00:19:33,381
Nolan Sorrento takes over the world.

288
00:19:33,548 --> 00:19:37,719
A real gunter would risk everything
to save the OASIS from IOI.

289
00:19:37,886 --> 00:19:39,220
Who said that?

290
00:19:39,387 --> 00:19:40,805
Me.

291
00:19:43,058 --> 00:19:44,601
There you go. Good as new.

292
00:19:45,185 --> 00:19:47,437
Thanks for the fix-up, my man.

293
00:19:57,197 --> 00:19:58,740
That's better.

294
00:19:59,282 --> 00:20:03,244
I'll wave to you
from the finish line, McFly.

295
00:20:06,664 --> 00:20:07,749
(CHUCKLES) That went well.

296
00:20:07,916 --> 00:20:09,626
Thanks to you, Captain Big Mouth.

297
00:20:09,793 --> 00:20:13,129
AUNT ALICE: <i>Wade? Wade?
Where the hell are my gloves?</i>

298
00:20:13,296 --> 00:20:15,256
Shit. I gotta go.

299
00:20:18,426 --> 00:20:19,427
ANNOUNCER: <i>X1.</i>

300
00:20:19,511 --> 00:20:23,056
When I'm after gold on Planet Doom,
I need every edge I can get.

301
00:20:23,348 --> 00:20:27,102
Every push, punch, gunshot,
you feel it all.

302
00:20:27,268 --> 00:20:31,439
ANNOUNCER: <i>Get ready for the feel,
the feel of real. X1.</i>

303
00:20:31,606 --> 00:20:33,858
PLAYER:
<i>The X1 is like wearing a second skin.</i>

304
00:20:33,942 --> 00:20:35,902
<i>A skin that kicks ass.</i>

305
00:20:37,654 --> 00:20:40,407
I zeroed out 'cause
of your broke-ass gloves.

306
00:20:40,573 --> 00:20:41,825
Who told you to use them?

307
00:20:41,991 --> 00:20:44,077
You took hers.

308
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:46,496
So you lost a death match.

309
00:20:46,663 --> 00:20:50,917
Why don't you just respawn
and level up like everyone else?

310
00:20:51,084 --> 00:20:52,210
You don't get it.

311
00:20:52,377 --> 00:20:55,296
I bought all these power-ups
for this challenge, and I lost it all.

312
00:20:55,463 --> 00:20:57,173
That artifact
was gonna pay for the house!

313
00:20:57,340 --> 00:20:58,341
AUNT ALICE: Wait.

314
00:20:58,508 --> 00:21:01,928
How much of our house money
did you spend on upgrades?

315
00:21:03,012 --> 00:21:05,765
Well, all of it, but I was gonna win.

316
00:21:05,890 --> 00:21:08,768
(SIGHS) That was our ticket out of here.

317
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:12,480
(SOBBING) You idiot.

318
00:21:12,647 --> 00:21:14,774
No, but I only lost 'cause
of the bad gloves.

319
00:21:14,941 --> 00:21:16,526
Our house! Our goddamn house!

320
00:21:16,693 --> 00:21:17,861
WADE: My boys were in that challenge.

321
00:21:18,027 --> 00:21:20,071
You couldn't have beat them
in a bootsuit, you noob.

322
00:21:20,697 --> 00:21:23,700
Stop! No! No!

323
00:21:23,867 --> 00:21:24,993
Alice, call the police!

324
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:26,661
No, we are not calling the cops.

325
00:21:26,828 --> 00:21:28,538
Go to your room, Rick.

326
00:21:28,705 --> 00:21:30,039
Come on, Alice.

327
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:34,377
Why do you put up with this guy?
He's a shitshow.

328
00:21:35,044 --> 00:21:39,466
I ought to kick the both of you out.
I swear to G-O-D, Wade Watts,

329
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:42,218
if I catch you touching my stuff again,

330
00:21:42,385 --> 00:21:44,929
not joking... Out.

331
00:21:51,853 --> 00:21:54,022
WADE: <i>"Wade Watts."</i>

332
00:21:54,189 --> 00:21:55,190
<i>My dad picked that name</i>

333
00:21:55,356 --> 00:21:57,609
<i>because it sounded
like a superhero's alter ego,</i>

334
00:21:58,193 --> 00:22:00,820
<i>like Peter Parker or Bruce Banner.</i>

335
00:22:01,863 --> 00:22:03,781
<i>But he died when I was a kid.</i>

336
00:22:03,948 --> 00:22:06,993
<i>My mom, too, and I ended up here,</i>

337
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:08,870
<i>living with Aunt Alice</i>

338
00:22:09,037 --> 00:22:11,414
<i>and her endless string
of hard-loving losers.</i>

339
00:22:14,292 --> 00:22:17,003
<i>"Halliday hated making rules."</i>

340
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:19,756
<i>Why is that line sticking in my head?</i>

341
00:22:22,133 --> 00:22:25,053
<i>Maybe it's 'cause Art3mis said it,
and she's hot.</i>

342
00:22:25,678 --> 00:22:27,764
<i>Maybe it's because she called me out,</i>

343
00:22:27,931 --> 00:22:30,225
<i>sitting here
in my tiny corner of nowhere,</i>

344
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:33,686
<i>protecting my small slice of nothing.</i>

345
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:35,939
<i>Or maybe...</i>

346
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:38,441
<i>Maybe it's because
that line means something</i>

347
00:22:38,608 --> 00:22:40,109
<i>and I missed it.</i>

348
00:22:40,318 --> 00:22:41,402
(POP MUSIC PLAYING)

349
00:22:43,112 --> 00:22:46,074
<i>The day the contest was announced,
the Halliday Journals appeared.</i>

350
00:22:46,241 --> 00:22:50,036
<i>He told us to look in his brain.
This was the next best thing.</i>

351
00:22:50,203 --> 00:22:53,540
<i>At first, it was jammed
with gunters looking for answers.</i>

352
00:22:53,706 --> 00:22:56,167
<i>Now, the once-crowded halls
of Halliday's memories</i>

353
00:22:56,334 --> 00:22:57,418
<i>are left to people like me.</i>

354
00:22:57,585 --> 00:23:00,213
Parzival. Oh, joy!

355
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:03,466
And how will you eat up
my valuable search time today?

356
00:23:03,883 --> 00:23:05,760
Gregarious Games, 2029... Office party.

357
00:23:06,052 --> 00:23:09,055
Office party. Yes, you've only seen it
a thousand times.

358
00:23:09,222 --> 00:23:11,140
Why not go back?

359
00:23:11,975 --> 00:23:15,520
Each entry into Halliday's Journals
is meticulously assembled

360
00:23:15,687 --> 00:23:18,022
from personal photographs,
home video recordings,

361
00:23:18,189 --> 00:23:19,941
surveillance, and nanny cams.

362
00:23:20,108 --> 00:23:23,778
All rendered into a
three-dimensional virtual experience.

363
00:23:23,945 --> 00:23:27,490
Also, Halliday archived every film,
game, book, and television program

364
00:23:27,615 --> 00:23:30,535
he ever saw, located on the mezzanine.

365
00:23:30,952 --> 00:23:34,372
No weapons or mature-themed avatars
are permitted within the Journals.

366
00:23:34,539 --> 00:23:37,834
Please enjoy your time with us,
and happy gunting!

367
00:23:38,334 --> 00:23:40,003
HALLIDAY: I like cleaning up.

368
00:23:40,169 --> 00:23:42,547
MORROW: Okay, Jim, I'm going.

369
00:23:47,510 --> 00:23:49,929
Everything changes, Jim.
Everything evolves.

370
00:23:50,471 --> 00:23:53,683
HALLIDAY: Some things are perfect
just the way they are. <i>Asteroids.</i>

371
00:23:53,850 --> 00:23:57,854
People don't live inside
an <i>Asteroids</i> arcade cabinet.

372
00:23:59,230 --> 00:24:00,440
I know that.

373
00:24:00,607 --> 00:24:03,151
Yeah, well, people are living inside
the arcade we built.

374
00:24:03,318 --> 00:24:05,194
- I built.
- Uh, well... (SIGHS)

375
00:24:05,486 --> 00:24:08,031
Right. Well, I guess you can say
whatever you want.

376
00:24:08,197 --> 00:24:09,240
I don't really wanna
talk about it anymore.

377
00:24:09,407 --> 00:24:10,742
No, of course
you don't wanna talk about it.

378
00:24:10,908 --> 00:24:11,909
You're forcing me out.

379
00:24:12,327 --> 00:24:13,369
Closer on Halliday.

380
00:24:13,786 --> 00:24:15,580
Look, invention
comes with responsibilities

381
00:24:15,747 --> 00:24:17,248
you didn't ask for.

382
00:24:17,915 --> 00:24:19,959
All right, if you make something
people want or need

383
00:24:20,126 --> 00:24:22,754
then it's up to you to set the limits.
You have to make some rules.

384
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:24,213
(WHISPERS)
"I don't wanna make any more rules."

385
00:24:24,505 --> 00:24:26,257
I don't wanna make any more rules.

386
00:24:26,341 --> 00:24:27,383
"I'm a dreamer."

387
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:28,801
I'm a dreamer.

388
00:24:29,093 --> 00:24:30,887
- I build worlds.
- "I build worlds."

389
00:24:32,013 --> 00:24:34,641
We created something beautiful, Jim,
but it's changed.

390
00:24:34,807 --> 00:24:36,267
Okay? It's really not a game anymore.

391
00:24:36,434 --> 00:24:37,769
Are we finished?

392
00:24:38,061 --> 00:24:42,523
I liked how things were
when they were...

393
00:24:44,025 --> 00:24:45,109
When it was a game.

394
00:24:45,276 --> 00:24:48,821
And we're back to where we started.
But that's the point, isn't it?

395
00:24:48,988 --> 00:24:51,199
Things move forward
whether you like it or not.

396
00:24:51,491 --> 00:24:53,534
Yeah, we're finished.

397
00:24:53,618 --> 00:24:55,244
MORROW: (SCOFFS) Fine.

398
00:24:57,497 --> 00:25:01,250
HALLIDAY: Why can't we go backwards,
for once?

399
00:25:03,628 --> 00:25:07,298
Backwards, really fast.
Fast as we can. (LAUGHS)

400
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:09,759
Really put the pedal to the metal,
you know?

401
00:25:09,926 --> 00:25:12,136
Go back 10 seconds!

402
00:25:12,637 --> 00:25:16,391
Why can't we go backwards, for once?

403
00:25:17,266 --> 00:25:21,187
Backwards, really fast.
Fast as we can. (LAUGHS)

404
00:25:21,688 --> 00:25:24,399
Really put the pedal to the metal,
you know?

405
00:25:25,483 --> 00:25:26,943
Bill and Ted did it.

406
00:25:27,276 --> 00:25:29,779
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

407
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:50,591
Back again so soon?

408
00:25:52,218 --> 00:25:54,345
Careful not to lose your shit.

409
00:25:58,433 --> 00:26:00,143
You figured something out.

410
00:26:00,810 --> 00:26:02,979
- Parzival, tell me.
- (HORN BLARES)

411
00:26:04,772 --> 00:26:05,857
(ENGINE REVS)

412
00:26:06,524 --> 00:26:07,567
(HORN BLARING)

413
00:26:30,381 --> 00:26:31,883
(TIRES SCREECHING)

414
00:26:52,820 --> 00:26:54,947
(ROARING)

415
00:27:06,375 --> 00:27:07,960
(ROARING)

416
00:27:17,261 --> 00:27:18,346
(ROARS)

417
00:27:23,768 --> 00:27:26,187
(TIRES SCREECHING)

418
00:27:26,312 --> 00:27:28,439
(INSTRUMENTS PLAYING TRIUMPHANT MUSIC)

419
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:47,041
Nice racing, Padawan.
You're the first to finish.

420
00:27:47,959 --> 00:27:52,421
(STAMMERING)
Mr. Halliday... Anorak.

421
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:55,091
It's such an honor.

422
00:27:55,383 --> 00:27:57,635
The honor is all mine.

423
00:28:08,771 --> 00:28:10,523
Get yourself a clue.

424
00:28:25,079 --> 00:28:28,541
Who is this Parzival,
and how the hell is he winning?

425
00:28:28,708 --> 00:28:31,168
Well, here's a better question.
Who cares?

426
00:28:31,335 --> 00:28:33,170
Halliday's contest is vitally important.

427
00:28:33,337 --> 00:28:36,382
I mean, it's nothing less than a war
for control of the future.

428
00:28:36,549 --> 00:28:39,594
But this Parzival?
He's not even clanned up.

429
00:28:39,760 --> 00:28:42,930
He's alone. We have an army.

430
00:28:43,097 --> 00:28:44,682
EXECUTIVE: And yet,
he's got the first key.

431
00:28:44,849 --> 00:28:46,267
Yeah, he has a key,

432
00:28:46,434 --> 00:28:49,562
but you have to get three of 'em
to win the contest.

433
00:28:49,729 --> 00:28:52,231
Our stock dove 6% yesterday.

434
00:28:52,398 --> 00:28:56,193
Loyalty division is reporting
profits of 28%. F'Nale.

435
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:59,030
We're opening
five new loyalty centers this month.

436
00:28:59,196 --> 00:29:01,073
Debt Services dwarfs Hardware.

437
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,117
Now, you really wanna talk to me
about stock prices?

438
00:29:03,284 --> 00:29:04,410
The shareholders won't be happy.

439
00:29:04,577 --> 00:29:07,830
It's not our job to make them happy.
It's our job to make them money,

440
00:29:07,997 --> 00:29:12,043
but once we launch this little baby,
they're gonna flip.

441
00:29:13,377 --> 00:29:16,422
We call this Pure O2.

442
00:29:16,589 --> 00:29:18,257
This is the first
of our planned upgrades.

443
00:29:18,424 --> 00:29:20,927
Once we can roll back
some of Halliday's ad restrictions,

444
00:29:21,093 --> 00:29:24,972
we estimate we can sell up to 80%

445
00:29:25,139 --> 00:29:30,394
of an individual's visual field before
inducing seizures, so picture this...

446
00:29:30,561 --> 00:29:33,564
All of this implies we win the contest.

447
00:29:36,525 --> 00:29:38,611
Indeed, it does.

448
00:29:38,694 --> 00:29:39,862
(MUSIC PLAYING)

449
00:29:40,279 --> 00:29:43,157
Dude, you won the key and 100,000 coins?

450
00:29:43,282 --> 00:29:44,325
As soon as I took the key,

451
00:29:44,408 --> 00:29:45,785
all the coins
just appeared in my account.

452
00:29:45,952 --> 00:29:48,955
I'll tell you what,
I'm soiling my haptics right now.

453
00:29:52,625 --> 00:29:54,251
What the hell's a Cataclyst?

454
00:29:54,418 --> 00:29:58,005
A bomb. Kills every avatar on a planet,
even the owner.

455
00:29:58,172 --> 00:29:59,173
AECH: Who'd want that?

456
00:29:59,340 --> 00:30:01,425
WADE: IOI. They buy everything.

457
00:30:02,802 --> 00:30:05,429
Twenty-thou for the holy hand grenade?

458
00:30:05,596 --> 00:30:07,264
That's a steal!

459
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:13,270
Whoa! Zemeckis Cube!
I need one of those.

460
00:30:13,437 --> 00:30:15,106
AECH: Okay, don't spend all your money.

461
00:30:18,776 --> 00:30:21,070
- X1 haptic bootsuit.
- (BEEPING)

462
00:30:35,710 --> 00:30:37,128
Oh, yeah!

463
00:31:30,181 --> 00:31:33,309
I-R0k, old friend. How are you?

464
00:31:35,561 --> 00:31:37,063
To be honest,
I have kind of a neck thing.

465
00:31:37,229 --> 00:31:39,023
It's like a carpel-tunnel deal

466
00:31:39,190 --> 00:31:40,900
but with your neck,
if that's even a thing.

467
00:31:41,067 --> 00:31:43,527
So if you could just stand
to your right.

468
00:31:43,694 --> 00:31:44,904
My right, your left.

469
