Whoa!

716
00:44:51,982 --> 00:44:53,650
Ow! Whoa.

717
00:44:58,154 --> 00:45:01,783
I don't think this is it.
No scoreboard, no obstacles.

718
00:45:01,950 --> 00:45:04,578
- Maybe a dance challenge?
- Whoa!

719
00:45:15,922 --> 00:45:17,132
(MUSIC STOPS)

720
00:45:17,299 --> 00:45:19,259
(<i>STAYIN' ALIVE</i> PLAYING)

721
00:45:20,093 --> 00:45:22,053
Old-school!

722
00:45:45,452 --> 00:45:46,620
You come prepared?

723
00:45:46,786 --> 00:45:47,996
"Prepared"?

724
00:45:51,625 --> 00:45:54,044
What kind of haptics you rockin'?

725
00:45:54,210 --> 00:45:56,546
You got the gloves
and full visor, or a full body?

726
00:46:00,634 --> 00:46:02,052
Can you feel this?

727
00:46:05,096 --> 00:46:06,348
Um, yeah.

728
00:46:06,514 --> 00:46:09,893
I got the X1 haptic bootsuit
with the microfiber crotch inlay.

729
00:46:10,060 --> 00:46:11,436
(LAUGHS)

730
00:46:22,322 --> 00:46:25,241
My, Parzival, you did come prepared.

731
00:46:28,620 --> 00:46:31,289
So, I've been thinking.

732
00:46:32,207 --> 00:46:34,668
Maybe it'd be cool if
we met up in the real world.

733
00:46:34,834 --> 00:46:36,252
No, you'd be disappointed.

734
00:46:36,419 --> 00:46:38,880
No, I wouldn't. I like you.

735
00:46:39,047 --> 00:46:41,132
You don't even know me.

736
00:46:41,299 --> 00:46:42,968
This isn't what I really look like.

737
00:46:43,134 --> 00:46:46,972
This isn't my real body,
or my real face.

738
00:46:47,138 --> 00:46:48,682
I don't care.

739
00:46:48,848 --> 00:46:50,058
I wanna know your real name.

740
00:46:53,937 --> 00:46:55,063
(ART3MIS LAUGHING)

741
00:47:03,655 --> 00:47:05,115
- My name's Wade.
- What?

742
00:47:06,658 --> 00:47:08,451
- I said my name's...
- Stop!

743
00:47:08,618 --> 00:47:11,329
Well, Buckaroo blows it. Shocking.

744
00:47:11,496 --> 00:47:13,957
Are you crazy?
You don't tell anyone who you are.

745
00:47:14,124 --> 00:47:15,458
You can't use your real name.

746
00:47:15,625 --> 00:47:16,710
You're not just anyone.

747
00:47:16,876 --> 00:47:17,961
You don't know me.

748
00:47:18,128 --> 00:47:19,754
You don't know anything about me.
We've never met.

749
00:47:19,921 --> 00:47:21,673
I do know you, Arty.

750
00:47:23,466 --> 00:47:24,968
I'm in love with you.

751
00:47:33,518 --> 00:47:34,853
- Is this part of the challenge?
- No.

752
00:47:35,895 --> 00:47:37,063
- It's an ambush.
- (COCKS GUN)

753
00:47:38,231 --> 00:47:39,315
(GROANS)

754
00:47:44,571 --> 00:47:46,698
IOI, always in the way.

755
00:47:47,323 --> 00:47:48,992
Did you hear what I said?
I said I'm in love with you.

756
00:47:49,159 --> 00:47:50,535
No, you're not.

757
00:47:52,120 --> 00:47:53,580
You only know what I want you to know.

758
00:47:53,747 --> 00:47:55,582
You only see what I want you to see.

759
00:47:58,543 --> 00:48:00,336
That's what you're in love with.

760
00:48:14,225 --> 00:48:15,351
Watch out!

761
00:48:16,895 --> 00:48:18,104
(GROANS)

762
00:48:22,901 --> 00:48:24,110
(YELLING)

763
00:48:25,612 --> 00:48:27,030
Pull.

764
00:48:29,491 --> 00:48:30,533
(GROANS)

765
00:48:34,079 --> 00:48:35,538
(BOTH GRUNTING)

766
00:48:39,667 --> 00:48:42,712
Head back! Z! Your armor is running low.

767
00:48:42,879 --> 00:48:44,005
I just bought this.

768
00:48:44,756 --> 00:48:45,882
(GRUNTS)

769
00:48:52,097 --> 00:48:53,223
Zemeckis Cube.

770
00:48:53,389 --> 00:48:55,225
Turns everything
back in time 60 seconds.

771
00:48:59,854 --> 00:49:01,856
And you waited until now to use it?

772
00:49:09,989 --> 00:49:12,117
Wow, you were amazing.

773
00:49:12,784 --> 00:49:13,910
(GROANS)

774
00:49:15,286 --> 00:49:17,455
(PANTING) This isn't a game, Z.

775
00:49:18,790 --> 00:49:20,583
I'm doing this to stop IOI.

776
00:49:20,750 --> 00:49:23,086
I'm talking
about real-world consequences.

777
00:49:23,253 --> 00:49:24,671
People suffering.

778
00:49:24,838 --> 00:49:26,047
- Actual life-and-death stuff.
- I know. I know...

779
00:49:26,214 --> 00:49:30,677
No, you don't know!
My dad died in a loyalty center.

780
00:49:31,636 --> 00:49:34,347
He borrowed gear.
(SNIFFLES) He built up debt.

781
00:49:34,806 --> 00:49:38,143
He moved in with the promise of
working it off, but he never did.

782
00:49:38,309 --> 00:49:40,019
IOI just raised his living expenses,

783
00:49:40,186 --> 00:49:41,604
then he got sick,
and he couldn't afford to get out.

784
00:49:41,771 --> 00:49:43,481
And then he died!

785
00:49:44,274 --> 00:49:45,275
I'm so sorry, I didn't...

786
00:49:45,441 --> 00:49:47,569
No, you don't live in the real world, Z.

787
00:49:47,735 --> 00:49:50,488
From what you've told me,
I don't think you ever have.

788
00:49:50,822 --> 00:49:54,242
You live inside this... This illusion,

789
00:49:54,409 --> 00:49:56,411
and I can't afford
to let you distract me.

790
00:50:09,174 --> 00:50:11,342
How the hell did they get away?

791
00:50:11,426 --> 00:50:13,553
<i>Do you want the long version?
Your guys suck.</i>

792
00:50:13,720 --> 00:50:15,263
<i>They failed to kill his avatar,</i>

793
00:50:15,430 --> 00:50:17,515
<i>which, if we're offering
constructive criticism,</i>

794
00:50:17,682 --> 00:50:20,351
<i>was a lame idea
and only would've slowed him down.</i>

795
00:50:20,518 --> 00:50:24,689
<i>Whereas my plan, which was cool
because I rock, actually worked.</i>

796
00:50:24,856 --> 00:50:26,274
He's still on the board.

797
00:50:26,441 --> 00:50:29,986
<i>I know that, Nolan.
But he won't be for long.</i>

798
00:50:30,153 --> 00:50:31,946
<i>I did a search for all the Wades</i>

799
00:50:32,113 --> 00:50:34,157
<i>who had recently bought an X1 bootsuit,</i>

800
00:50:34,324 --> 00:50:37,368
<i>cross-referenced that</i>
<i>with public records, and</i> voilà,

801
00:50:37,535 --> 00:50:41,539
<i>which is French for...
"And then I found out."</i>

802
00:50:42,165 --> 00:50:43,333
<i>Ready?</i>

803
00:50:43,499 --> 00:50:48,171
<i>The real-world identity of Paival
is Wade Watts.</i>

804
00:50:48,963 --> 00:50:50,506
<i>Voilà.</i>

805
00:50:52,217 --> 00:50:54,385
Are you loyal, Ms. Zandor?

806
00:50:55,094 --> 00:50:56,721
You really want me to answer that?

807
00:50:56,888 --> 00:50:58,264
(CLEARS THROAT)
Well, when you're at war,

808
00:50:58,431 --> 00:51:00,516
you need people
who are loyal to a fault.

809
00:51:01,476 --> 00:51:03,186
People you can count on
to get things done.

810
00:51:03,353 --> 00:51:05,855
I just get people arrested
for not paying their bills.

811
00:51:06,022 --> 00:51:08,775
Yeah, 'cause there are some problems
that require a physical solution,

812
00:51:08,942 --> 00:51:11,361
but there are other times,
particularly at war,

813
00:51:11,527 --> 00:51:13,071
when you need a different set of rules.

814
00:51:13,238 --> 00:51:14,572
- The rules of war.
- Exactly.

815
00:51:14,739 --> 00:51:17,492
It's too bad my division doesn't operate
inside the OASIS.

816
00:51:17,659 --> 00:51:20,411
Yeah, but if this war
remains in the OASIS,

817
00:51:20,578 --> 00:51:22,038
then you can't do anything.

818
00:51:22,956 --> 00:51:25,750
So, this is one of those conversations
that we're not really having.

819
00:51:25,917 --> 00:51:27,502
Well, we've had
these kind of conversations before,

820
00:51:27,669 --> 00:51:28,670
and look where you are now.

821
00:51:28,836 --> 00:51:31,256
You got a seat on the board,
head of your own division,

822
00:51:31,422 --> 00:51:35,218
a division that will cease to exist
if the wrong person wins this contest.

823
00:51:35,385 --> 00:51:38,554
F'Nale, a game decides our fate.

824
00:51:38,721 --> 00:51:42,475
The only question is,
how far are we willing to go to win it?

825
00:51:44,686 --> 00:51:46,729
Tell me what you need, Nolan.

826
00:51:57,573 --> 00:51:59,701
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

827
00:52:12,463 --> 00:52:14,340
(BEEPING)

828
00:53:05,099 --> 00:53:06,601
Whoa.

829
00:53:10,438 --> 00:53:11,439
Where am I?

830
00:53:11,606 --> 00:53:14,359
IOI Plaza.
You're a hologram in the real world.

831
00:53:15,276 --> 00:53:16,486
That's a really cool rig.

832
00:53:16,652 --> 00:53:20,823
Thank you.
It's a brand-new Habashaw, OIR 9400.

833
00:53:20,990 --> 00:53:22,700
It looks like a giant hamster ball.

834
00:53:22,867 --> 00:53:27,580
You know, if you came to work at IOI,
you'd get one of these.

835
00:53:27,747 --> 00:53:28,956
I don't clan up.

836
00:53:29,123 --> 00:53:31,751
You'd also get your own
penthouse apartment in Columbus

837
00:53:31,918 --> 00:53:34,045
with the highest-speed connection.

838
00:53:34,212 --> 00:53:39,133
In the OASIS, you'd get unlimited
weapons, magic items, ships.

839
00:53:39,217 --> 00:53:41,302
You want the ship from <i>Defender?</i>

840
00:53:41,469 --> 00:53:44,055
You know, the kind
that can just jump into hyperspace?

841
00:53:44,222 --> 00:53:46,057
You want the <i>Millennium Falcon?</i>

842
00:53:47,016 --> 00:53:48,017
You have that?

843
00:53:48,101 --> 00:53:51,145
Anything you need
to help you find that egg,

844
00:53:51,312 --> 00:53:52,605
and then there's the salary.

845
00:53:53,773 --> 00:53:55,733
Four million a year.

846
00:53:55,900 --> 00:53:59,320
And if you do happen to find
that Easter egg, there's a bonus.

847
00:53:59,487 --> 00:54:01,739
Twenty-five million dollars.

848
00:54:03,282 --> 00:54:06,035
(PANTING)

849
00:54:07,161 --> 00:54:10,581
I can see you're using
emotion-suppressing software right now,

850
00:54:10,748 --> 00:54:13,584
and why wouldn't you?
It's smart, not to show your hand.

851
00:54:19,090 --> 00:54:22,760
It is a lot of money.
I could really use it.

852
00:54:27,765 --> 00:54:29,976
But I don't think you and I
would have the same plans.

853
00:54:30,143 --> 00:54:33,020
Well, I don't know about that.
What, for the OASIS?

854
00:54:33,187 --> 00:54:36,315
I guess
if you're not a John Hughes fan...

855
00:54:37,483 --> 00:54:39,068
Of course I am.

856
00:54:39,235 --> 00:54:41,696
Because the first thing that I would do

857
00:54:41,863 --> 00:54:45,450
is convert all the schools
on Ludus to replicas

858
00:54:45,616 --> 00:54:48,619
from <i>The Breakfast Club</i>
and <i>Ferris Bueller.</i>

859
00:54:48,786 --> 00:54:51,038
No way. That's a great idea.

860
00:54:51,956 --> 00:54:54,250
Which school, Ridgemont or Faber?

861
00:54:54,417 --> 00:54:57,336
<i>Fast Times at Ridgemont High,</i>
not John Hughes.

862
00:54:57,503 --> 00:55:00,590
It's a trap.
Faber College from <i>Animal House.</i>

863
00:55:00,756 --> 00:55:02,049
John Hughes didn't direct

864
00:55:02,216 --> 00:55:04,760
<i>Fast Times at Ridgemont High</i>
or <i>Animal House.</i>

865
00:55:05,386 --> 00:55:08,556
<i>Ferris Bueller</i> and <i>The Breakfast Club,</i>
they went to Shermer High School,

866
00:55:08,723 --> 00:55:11,476
which is in Shermer, Illinois.
I know what you think.

867
00:55:12,268 --> 00:55:13,811
You think I'm a corporate asshole,

868
00:55:13,978 --> 00:55:16,189
that I don't appreciate
pop culture, but...

869
00:55:17,356 --> 00:55:20,318
Man, that's not true.
You know, when I wanna blow off steam...

870
00:55:20,485 --> 00:55:24,280
Drink Tab, play <i>Robotron,</i>
listen to Duran Duran.

871
00:55:24,447 --> 00:55:25,865
I crack open a Tab.

872
00:55:26,032 --> 00:55:28,284
I put on some Duran Duran.
I play <i>Robotron.</i>

873
00:55:28,451 --> 00:55:30,411
That's why I love the OASIS.

874
00:55:30,578 --> 00:55:33,748
'Cause it's just full
of all these things, man,

875
00:55:33,915 --> 00:55:35,374
that people love. You know?

876
00:55:43,257 --> 00:55:45,593
I'm a businessman. I get it.

877
00:55:45,760 --> 00:55:48,387
But I gotta do my job.

878
00:55:48,554 --> 00:55:53,309
(SOFTLY) But I didn't ask you here
just to help us find the egg, Parzival.

879
00:55:54,310 --> 00:55:58,064
I asked you here for what comes after.

880
00:55:59,315 --> 00:56:00,942
What would Halliday say?

881
00:56:02,026 --> 00:56:04,695
James Halliday is dead.

882
00:56:05,988 --> 00:56:08,908
Yeah. He is.

883
00:56:09,992 --> 00:56:13,829
All that's left of him is this contest.
And you know what?

884
00:56:14,914 --> 00:56:17,124
It just seems like
he wouldn't want you winning it.

885
00:56:17,291 --> 00:56:18,459
A fanboy knows a hater,

886
00:56:18,626 --> 00:56:21,212
and I know you've got a whole department
of oologists in your ear.

887
00:56:21,379 --> 00:56:23,464
So, if you wanna know
what I really think...

888
00:56:23,631 --> 00:56:25,091
I think you're full of shit.

889
00:56:30,471 --> 00:56:31,556
Here's my offer.

890
00:56:31,722 --> 00:56:33,474
Your board of directors,
you got them in the other ear?

891
00:56:33,641 --> 00:56:35,518
Why don't you tell 'em this.

892
00:56:36,727 --> 00:56:39,146
If they dump you, I'll consider it.

893
00:56:39,522 --> 00:56:41,566
I might say something off the record.

894
00:56:42,608 --> 00:56:44,110
I had to make the offer.

895
00:56:44,277 --> 00:56:47,488
The board expected it,
but I was really hoping you'd say no.

896
00:56:47,655 --> 00:56:50,908
Because if anyone's gonna win
this competition, it's me.

897
00:56:51,075 --> 00:56:52,451
My avatar gets the egg

898
00:56:52,618 --> 00:56:56,205
'cause I'm the only one here
with the balls to run this place.

899
00:56:56,497 --> 00:56:58,833
Wow, you really switched gears there.

900
00:56:59,000 --> 00:57:01,377
From fairly reasonable
to maniacal overlord.

901
00:57:02,086 --> 00:57:04,005
You should be grateful, Wade.

902
00:57:05,089 --> 00:57:08,259
<i>You won't be around
to endure my maniacal reign.</i>

903
00:57:08,509 --> 00:57:10,136
Yeah, that's right. I know who you are.

904
00:57:10,303 --> 00:57:14,890
Wade Owen Watts, born August 12, 2027.

905
00:57:15,558 --> 00:57:19,395
I also know where you are.
Unit 56K, Columbus stacks.

906
00:57:19,562 --> 00:57:22,148
You were last seen entering your trailer
three days ago.

907
00:57:22,315 --> 00:57:23,691
You haven't left since.

908
00:57:23,858 --> 00:57:24,859
WADE: What are you doing? You can't...

909
00:57:25,026 --> 00:57:26,110
With all that's going on in the world,

910
00:57:26,277 --> 00:57:27,945
do you really think that
anyone's gonna give a damn

911
00:57:28,112 --> 00:57:29,113
about an explosion

912
00:57:29,280 --> 00:57:31,991
in some ghetto trash rat warren
in Columbus?

913
00:57:32,158 --> 00:57:34,243
Sorrento, don't do this.
I'm not even there!

914
00:57:34,410 --> 00:57:36,245
Not for long.

915
00:57:36,871 --> 00:57:38,414
(PANTING)

916
00:57:39,957 --> 00:57:42,001
Call Alice.

917
00:57:42,168 --> 00:57:43,836
Dial Alice.

918
00:58:07,485 --> 00:58:09,945
(RINGING)

919
00:58:10,363 --> 00:58:12,198
Pick up! Pick up! Alice!

920
00:58:13,824 --> 00:58:16,160
(CONTINUES RINGING)

921
00:58:17,328 --> 00:58:19,622
This bootsuit's pretty awesome.
Thanks for that.

922
00:58:19,789 --> 00:58:21,707
Rick! Rick, the place is gonna blow!

923
00:58:21,874 --> 00:58:23,209
Rick, is that Wade?

924
00:58:23,376 --> 00:58:25,419
- Put Alice on!
- Let me talk to him.

925
00:58:25,586 --> 00:58:27,505
Don't call here anymore, you got me?

926
00:58:27,588 --> 00:58:28,798
(PANTING)

927
00:58:28,964 --> 00:58:31,842
I don't wanna hear your voice
ever again.

928
00:58:37,723 --> 00:58:40,476
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

929
00:58:51,612 --> 00:58:53,280
(SIRENS WAILING)

930
00:59:07,336 --> 00:59:08,671
(BEEPING)

931
00:59:08,879 --> 00:59:12,425
Contact Aech, Daito, Sho, and Art3mis.

932
00:59:13,259 --> 00:59:15,302
IOI came for me in the real world.

933
00:59:15,469 --> 00:59:18,180
They gotta be coming after you,
so wherever you are...

934
00:59:18,264 --> 00:59:19,807
(MUFFLED GRUNTING)

935
00:59:35,531 --> 00:59:37,908
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

936
00:59:44,331 --> 00:59:46,208
Sorry about the blindfold.

937
00:59:46,375 --> 00:59:48,502
My guys are a little paranoid.

938
00:59:49,378 --> 00:59:50,963
Say that again.

939
00:59:51,589 --> 00:59:53,924
My guys are a little paranoid.

940
00:59:55,050 --> 00:59:56,469
Art3mis?

941
00:59:58,053 --> 01:00:02,057
My real name is Samantha,
but yeah, I'm Art3mis.

942
01:00:03,976 --> 01:00:06,645
Showers are that way,
clean clothes, too.

943
01:00:09,982 --> 01:00:13,986
Welcome to the rebellion, Wade.

944
01:00:25,206 --> 01:00:29,210
WADE: That's IOI.
So the stacks are over there?

945
01:00:30,711 --> 01:00:33,506
We've been living this close
to each other the whole time?

946
01:00:35,007 --> 01:00:36,300
Next door,

947
01:00:37,176 --> 01:00:41,222
around the world,
it's all the same in the OASIS.

948
01:00:43,724 --> 01:00:45,684
For the record,

949
01:00:46,143 --> 01:00:47,561
um...

950
01:00:47,645 --> 01:00:49,855
I'm not disappointed.

951
01:00:51,649 --> 01:00:54,568
You said I would be disappointed
when I met you, but...

952
01:00:54,735 --> 01:00:56,403
I'm not.

953
01:00:57,988 --> 01:01:00,741
I've lived with it my whole life.
You don't have to pretend.

954
01:01:15,339 --> 01:01:18,050
You have a birthmark, so what?

955
01:01:19,009 --> 01:01:20,678
Why would that scare me?

956
01:01:27,935 --> 01:01:30,187
Z, if I hurt you, I'm sorry.

957
01:01:30,563 --> 01:01:31,730
No, it's...

958
01:01:32,773 --> 01:01:35,109
Wait, did you just call me "Z"?

959
01:01:36,068 --> 01:01:38,028
- Oh, my God. Did I?
- I think you did.

960
01:01:38,112 --> 01:01:39,738
(LAUGHS) Wade, I'm sorry.

961
01:01:39,989 --> 01:01:42,157
Yeah, Wade, Z.

962
01:01:42,324 --> 01:01:45,452
You can call me whatever you want.
And I'll call you Sam.

963
01:01:45,619 --> 01:01:46,620
No.

964
01:01:47,746 --> 01:01:48,747
Samantha?

965
01:01:49,248 --> 01:01:51,458
Okay. Cool.

966
01:01:58,799 --> 01:02:00,509
Wow.

967
01:02:01,385 --> 01:02:03,429
It's so much slower here.

968
01:02:04,847 --> 01:02:08,142
I mean, the wind, the people...

969
01:02:10,060 --> 01:02:11,854
Everything.

970
01:02:17,109 --> 01:02:19,111
We forget what it's like to be outside.

971
01:02:19,570 --> 01:02:20,571
Yeah.

972
01:02:21,530 --> 01:02:23,073
(WADE CHUCKLES)

973
01:02:23,908 --> 01:02:26,285
- Uh...
- Oh, shit!

974
01:02:27,369 --> 01:02:28,871
- I just figured it out.
- Figured what out?

975
01:02:29,038 --> 01:02:30,414
The second clue. I know what it means.

976
01:02:36,795 --> 01:02:38,297
We've been thinking about it
too literally.

977
01:02:38,881 --> 01:02:39,882
"The leap not taken,"

978
01:02:40,049 --> 01:02:42,468
the leap Halliday didn't take,
is with Kira.

979
01:02:42,635 --> 01:02:46,305
Yeah, but... I mean, he blamed her
for breaking up him and Morrow.

980
01:02:46,472 --> 01:02:49,266
No. Halliday was madly in love with her.

981
01:02:49,433 --> 01:02:51,685
He had a chance with Kira.
He had a chance to kiss her, but...

982
01:02:51,852 --> 01:02:52,937
He didn't take the leap.

983
01:02:53,103 --> 01:02:55,773
Right. So that's where we go next.

984
01:02:56,941 --> 01:02:58,317
The place where the leap wasn't taken.

985
01:02:58,484 --> 01:02:59,485
Where the date was.

986
01:02:59,944 --> 01:03:01,570
At the movies!

987
01:03:02,321 --> 01:03:03,948
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)
- Hey, Curator.

988
01:03:04,114 --> 01:03:05,950
We figured out the second clue.
The challenge is here.

989
01:03:06,116 --> 01:03:07,993
Halliday kept track of every movie
he ever watched,

990
01:03:08,160 --> 01:03:11,080
the week and the year he watched it,
and how many times.

991
01:03:11,246 --> 01:03:15,334
Curator, can we see
November 23 to 27, 2025?

992
01:03:16,001 --> 01:03:17,795
That's the week
he went on the date with Kira.

993
01:03:22,424 --> 01:03:25,886
Okay, so our options for that week
are <i>The Fly</i> remake.

994
01:03:26,053 --> 01:03:28,013
Great flick, terrible date movie.

995
01:03:28,180 --> 01:03:30,766
<i>Say Anything...</i> That would make sense.

996
01:03:31,684 --> 01:03:36,063
We gotta remember the clue.
"A creator who hates his own creation."

997
01:03:40,734 --> 01:03:42,528
<i>The Shining!</i>

998
01:03:42,695 --> 01:03:44,822
It's Halliday's
11th favorite horror film,

999
01:03:44,989 --> 01:03:47,282
and it's based on the best-selling book
by Stephen King,

1000
01:03:47,366 --> 01:03:48,367
who hated the movie!

1001
01:03:48,993 --> 01:03:50,911
Hey! No side chitchat.

1002
01:03:51,078 --> 01:03:52,371
I think we found it.

1003
01:03:54,540 --> 01:03:56,083
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

1004
01:03:56,166 --> 01:03:58,711
Are you absolutely sure
you want to go here?

1005
01:03:58,877 --> 01:04:00,587
Absolutely positive.

1006
01:04:00,754 --> 01:04:03,173
Let's hope you have the belly for it.

1007
01:04:03,590 --> 01:04:04,675
(ALL GASP)

1008
01:04:13,100 --> 01:04:16,645
(THEME FROM <i>THE SHINING</i> PLAYING)

1009
01:04:46,550 --> 01:04:47,634
Look.

1010
01:04:49,136 --> 01:04:51,138
Ticking clock.

1011
01:04:51,305 --> 01:04:54,058
Okay, so I'm estimating about

1012
01:04:55,142 --> 01:04:57,019
five minutes to find the key.

1013
01:04:57,186 --> 01:04:58,645
Yeah, there are so many keys
in <i>The Shining,</i> though.

1014
01:04:58,812 --> 01:05:00,230
Where do we start?

1015
01:05:01,648 --> 01:05:04,860
I've never seen <i>The Shining.</i>
Is it really scary?

1016
01:05:05,069 --> 01:05:08,238
Uh, I had to watch it
through my fingers.

1017
01:05:08,989 --> 01:05:11,325
WADE: Okay, so we got the key
from room 237,

1018
01:05:11,950 --> 01:05:13,702
the keys to the Snowcat,

1019
01:05:13,869 --> 01:05:15,537
or the keys they give Jack
at the beginning of the movie.

1020
01:05:15,704 --> 01:05:17,414
ART3MIS: Well,
if it's "the leap not taken,"

1021
01:05:17,498 --> 01:05:18,499
maybe the key isn't a key at all.

1022
01:05:18,665 --> 01:05:19,875
SHO: I know where the Snowcat keys are!

1023
01:05:20,042 --> 01:05:21,085
WADE: I say we split up.

1024
01:05:21,251 --> 01:05:22,252
We get all the keys

1025
01:05:22,377 --> 01:05:24,379
and then we meet back
at the Torrances' apartment.

1026
01:05:28,383 --> 01:05:30,010
BOTH: Hello, Danny.

1027
01:05:31,261 --> 01:05:32,888
Come play with us.

1028
01:05:33,055 --> 01:05:36,266
Little girls,
y'all know how to get out of here?

1029
01:05:41,271 --> 01:05:42,272
Wait, wait!

1030
01:05:42,439 --> 01:05:44,399
Wait, where's Aech?

1031
01:05:44,566 --> 01:05:45,818
AECH: Wait!

1032
01:05:46,944 --> 01:05:47,945
Aech!

1033
01:05:48,737 --> 01:05:49,780
No, no, no, no!

1034
01:05:56,203 --> 01:05:58,122
(SCREAMING)

1035
01:06:05,045 --> 01:06:06,630
(GROANS)

1036
01:06:08,006 --> 01:06:09,633
Ahh!

1037
01:06:10,300 --> 01:06:11,969
(GASPING)

1038
01:06:14,346 --> 01:06:15,931
Ahh!

1039
01:06:17,766 --> 01:06:19,601
(GRUNTING)

1040
01:06:29,820 --> 01:06:31,363
(PANTING)

1041
01:06:49,464 --> 01:06:52,176
Oh, uh, hi, naked lady. I'm sorry.

1042
01:06:52,342 --> 01:06:54,094
I didn't mean to interrupt,
uh, your bath time.

1043
01:06:54,428 --> 01:06:56,221
I know self-care can be important.

1044
01:06:56,430 --> 01:06:59,600
Uh, but can you do me a favor
and tell me, where are all the exits?

1045
01:07:03,228 --> 01:07:04,730
Huh. Whoa.

1046
01:07:04,813 --> 01:07:07,024
Okay, am I being punked?

1047
01:07:07,191 --> 01:07:09,526
'Cause you're likin' me
a little way too much.

1048
01:07:11,069 --> 01:07:13,197
All right, you know what?
I'ma go with it.

1049
01:07:17,201 --> 01:07:19,369
(WOMAN CACKLING)

1050
01:07:21,038 --> 01:07:23,749
(SCREAMING)

1051
01:07:24,833 --> 01:07:26,418
(GASPING)

1052
01:07:26,752 --> 01:07:27,794
Ahh!

1053
01:07:28,420 --> 01:07:29,588
(YELLING)

1054
01:07:29,880 --> 01:07:31,506
(CACKLING)

1055
01:07:34,134 --> 01:07:35,594
(YELLING)

1056
01:07:42,809 --> 01:07:45,103
(PANTING)

1057
01:07:46,021 --> 01:07:47,522
(CACKLING)

1058
01:07:50,984 --> 01:07:52,402
(WHIMPERS)

1059
01:07:56,949 --> 01:07:58,325
(SCREAMING)

1060
01:08:01,036 --> 01:08:03,121
(AECH PANTING)

1061
01:08:05,123 --> 01:08:06,375
Time's running out.

1062
01:08:06,541 --> 01:08:08,502
Yo, Z, is Art3mis pissed at me?

1063
01:08:08,669 --> 01:08:10,921
Dude, I'm pissed at you.
You've never seen <i>The Shining,</i> have you?

1064
01:08:11,088 --> 01:08:12,297
You know I hate scary movies!

1065
01:08:12,464 --> 01:08:13,465
We got the key.

1066
01:08:13,632 --> 01:08:14,883
Sweet! To room 237!

1067
01:08:15,050 --> 01:08:17,427
We ain't got no business
goin' to room 237!

1068
01:08:17,594 --> 01:08:18,595
We should stay out!

1069
01:08:18,762 --> 01:08:20,847
Plus, there was this crazy,
naked zombie lady in there.

1070
01:08:21,014 --> 01:08:22,516
There are no zombies in <i>The Shining.</i>

1071
01:08:22,683 --> 01:08:24,518
Well, maybe it's not supposed
to be like the movie.

1072
01:08:24,685 --> 01:08:26,228
Kira is the key.
You're the one who said it.

1073
01:08:26,395 --> 01:08:28,522
Hey, y'all. I saw a picture of Kira!

1074
01:08:28,605 --> 01:08:30,649
- ART3MIS: Huh?
- (ALL GROAN)

1075
01:08:33,193 --> 01:08:34,236
(STRAINING) Where?

1076
01:08:41,243 --> 01:08:44,538
ART3MIS: It's Kira. "Escape your past."

1077
01:08:45,372 --> 01:08:47,207
"The leap not taken."

1078
01:08:48,583 --> 01:08:50,419
Halliday's greatest fear
wasn't <i>The Shining</i>

1079
01:08:50,585 --> 01:08:52,004
or any book or movie.

1080
01:08:53,046 --> 01:08:55,841
His biggest fear was kissing a girl.

1081
01:08:56,633 --> 01:08:58,927
That's the leap he couldn't take.

1082
01:09:00,178 --> 01:09:01,888
(JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING IN THE DISTANCE)

1083
01:09:07,144 --> 01:09:08,770
The ballroom.

1084
01:09:17,738 --> 01:09:19,406
(JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)

1085
01:09:23,410 --> 01:09:25,495
- WADE: Aech, come on.
- (GRUNTS)

1086
01:09:29,082 --> 01:09:31,043
Zombies. Told you.

1087
01:09:32,502 --> 01:09:33,712
ART3MIS: That's her.

1088
01:09:34,838 --> 01:09:36,256
That's Kira.

1089
01:09:39,343 --> 01:09:40,510
None of this is in <i>The Shining.</i>

1090
01:09:40,677 --> 01:09:43,430
Z, look. That's the zombie-circle level
in <i>Mayhem Mansion,</i>

1091
01:09:43,597 --> 01:09:45,057
one of Halliday's first games.

1092
01:09:45,223 --> 01:09:47,017
The whole <i>Shining</i> trivia
is just a diversion.

1093
01:09:48,268 --> 01:09:49,853
One minute left.

1094
01:09:51,313 --> 01:09:52,481
How do we get to her?

1095
01:09:52,647 --> 01:09:53,648
Take the leap.

1096
01:09:53,815 --> 01:09:54,816
- Wait!
- (GRUNTS)

1097
01:09:56,234 --> 01:09:57,319
ALL: Whoa!

1098
01:09:59,821 --> 01:10:00,947
(GRUNTS)

1099
01:10:03,200 --> 01:10:05,869
Okay, Mr. Dead Guy. Cool if I lead?

1100
01:10:05,952 --> 01:10:07,037
(GROWLS)

1101
01:10:09,039 --> 01:10:10,415
(GRUNTING)

1102
01:10:15,420 --> 01:10:17,130
(PANTING)

1103
01:10:39,486 --> 01:10:41,321
- (GRUNTS)
- (GROANS)

1104
01:10:50,288 --> 01:10:51,665
(INHALES DEEPLY)

1105
01:10:53,583 --> 01:10:55,460
Care to dance?

1106
01:10:55,877 --> 01:10:59,339
Do you know how long
I've been waiting for you to ask?

1107
01:11:05,220 --> 01:11:07,639
Well, well, well.

1108
01:11:07,806 --> 01:11:12,185
So you found my Jade Key.

1109
01:11:14,688 --> 01:11:16,606
Imagine that.

1110
01:11:21,611 --> 01:11:23,155
Thank you.

1111
01:11:27,951 --> 01:11:29,995
- Kira was a very beautiful...
- Go on.

1112
01:11:59,065 --> 01:12:01,985
One of our oologists saw them
enter the media library.

1113
01:12:02,152 --> 01:12:03,653
She cracked the clue.

1114
01:12:03,820 --> 01:12:06,865
Now, we just have to win
<i>The Shining</i> challenge.

1115
01:12:07,616 --> 01:12:09,409
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1116
01:12:09,951 --> 01:12:12,662
Get her off me! Get her off me!

1117
01:12:12,746 --> 01:12:13,830
(WOMAN CACKLING)

1118
01:12:13,914 --> 01:12:15,040
(SHRIEKING)

1119
01:12:16,166 --> 01:12:17,792
(ALL SCREAMING)

1120
01:12:22,172 --> 01:12:26,676
Mr. Sorrento,
I really think you need to see this.

1121
01:12:28,803 --> 01:12:30,597
Now Parzival's got the Jade Key.

1122
01:12:41,024 --> 01:12:43,109
He's alive.

1123
01:12:43,401 --> 01:12:45,737
I know. I'll get back to you.

1124
01:12:46,363 --> 01:12:48,365
I got what you're looking for.

1125
01:12:52,285 --> 01:12:56,498
Freeze. This guy.
The one with the lame tattoo.

1126
01:12:57,082 --> 01:12:58,250
Enlarge.

1127
01:13:00,794 --> 01:13:03,880
Run him through our database,
every IOI drone in Columbus.

1128
01:13:04,047 --> 01:13:05,465
Find him.

1129
01:13:10,804 --> 01:13:13,014
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

1130
01:13:32,409 --> 01:13:33,994
Groceries are here.

1131
01:13:34,119 --> 01:13:35,245
All right. Gluten-O's...

1132
01:13:35,412 --> 01:13:36,705
SAMANTHA: "If you know
the answer ultimate,

1133
01:13:36,788 --> 01:13:37,998
"divide it by the number magic,

1134
01:13:38,164 --> 01:13:41,793
"and what you need, want, and desire
will be found in the fortress tragic."

1135
01:13:41,960 --> 01:13:43,962
"Tragic," that's gotta be Halliday
referring to himself.

1136
01:13:44,087 --> 01:13:45,088
Why?

1137
01:13:45,171 --> 01:13:46,298
Because he was lonely.

1138
01:13:46,464 --> 01:13:48,800
He had no one to spend his life with
towards the end.

1139
01:13:48,883 --> 01:13:49,884
Yeah, that's true.

1140
01:13:49,968 --> 01:13:52,762
The contest has gotta be somehow
about connecting with someone.

1141
01:13:52,929 --> 01:13:54,264
Anyone.

1142
01:13:54,431 --> 01:13:55,807
He wants the person
who cares for the OASIS

1143
01:13:55,974 --> 01:13:57,517
to be connected with the world.

1144
01:13:57,684 --> 01:14:00,145
That's what I think
he's trying to tell us.

1145
01:14:06,151 --> 01:14:07,777
Wade.

1146
01:14:09,821 --> 01:14:11,489
You understand Halliday.

1147
01:14:12,157 --> 01:14:14,659
You know him better than anyone.

1148
01:14:15,869 --> 01:14:18,413
It's exactly why I think you'll win.

1149
01:14:18,872 --> 01:14:22,667
Really? You really think I'm gonna win?

1150
01:14:23,918 --> 01:14:26,171
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1151
01:14:26,630 --> 01:14:28,340
MAN: Do not move!

1152
01:14:33,803 --> 01:14:35,221
Target identified!

1153
01:14:36,306 --> 01:14:37,849
Freeze! Don't move!

1154
01:14:44,731 --> 01:14:47,275
- This leads right to the alley.
- You first.

1155
01:14:47,359 --> 01:14:49,027
I'm right behind you. Go now!

1156
01:14:50,654 --> 01:14:52,072
Come on!

1157
01:14:52,238 --> 01:14:54,574
- Wade, the OASIS needs you.
- What?

1158
01:14:54,741 --> 01:14:55,867
- I'm gonna delay them.
- Wait!

1159
01:14:56,034 --> 01:14:57,827
No, no, no, wait! No, no, no!

1160
01:14:58,495 --> 01:15:00,664
You'll forgive me for this, I promise.

1161
01:15:09,881 --> 01:15:11,466
MAN: Freeze, freeze, freeze!

1162
01:15:12,509 --> 01:15:13,510
Don't move!

1163
01:15:18,807 --> 01:15:21,351
Samantha Evelyn Cook.

1164
01:15:21,518 --> 01:15:25,021
IOI has purchased and consolidated
all of your outstanding debt,

1165
01:15:25,188 --> 01:15:28,274
currently in excess of 23,000 credits.

1166
01:15:28,441 --> 01:15:31,111
You will be remanded to the nearest
IOI loyalty center

1167
01:15:31,319 --> 01:15:32,654
until your debt is paid in full,

1168
01:15:32,821 --> 01:15:35,448
including any interest, processing,

1169
01:15:35,615 --> 01:15:38,118
or late fees you incur henceforth.

1170
01:15:38,284 --> 01:15:40,453
MAN 1: Does anybody have eyes?
MAN 2: Check down the next street!

1171
01:15:53,299 --> 01:15:55,343
- "First to the key."
- "First to the egg."

1172
01:15:55,510 --> 01:15:56,803
Wait, what?

1173
01:15:57,804 --> 01:15:59,973
"Never trust someone you meet
in the OASIS."

1174
01:16:01,182 --> 01:16:03,643
"She might be a 300-pound dude
named Chuck..."

1175
01:16:03,810 --> 01:16:07,021
"Who lives in his mama's basement
in suburban Detroit."

1176
01:16:09,399 --> 01:16:10,400
Aech!

1177
01:16:11,317 --> 01:16:14,821
Helen. My dad called me Aech
It kinda stuck. Let's go!

1178
01:16:24,706 --> 01:16:26,875
That thing's IDing my van.

1179
01:16:32,380 --> 01:16:33,506
(YELLS)

1180
01:16:33,715 --> 01:16:35,383
(GRUNTING)

1181
01:16:41,723 --> 01:16:43,725
Come on. They've spotted us.

1182
01:16:44,559 --> 01:16:45,560
Daito.

1183
01:16:45,643 --> 01:16:48,813
My real name is Toshiro.
Samantha got us a message.

1184
01:16:48,980 --> 01:16:50,648
She told us to meet you here.

1185
01:16:50,815 --> 01:16:52,066
Samantha, they took her to the...

1186
01:16:52,233 --> 01:16:53,651
The loyalty center, I know.

1187
01:16:53,818 --> 01:16:57,030
Look, in other awesome news,
the Sixers found the third challenge.

1188
01:16:57,822 --> 01:16:59,574
- What?
- Just come on, get in!

1189
01:16:59,741 --> 01:17:00,742
All right. Let's go.

1190
01:17:00,867 --> 01:17:03,077
Hurry up. Go, go, go. All right.

1191
01:17:07,040 --> 01:17:08,500
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1192
01:17:14,839 --> 01:17:17,175
How did IOI find
the third challenge so fast?

1193
01:17:17,342 --> 01:17:19,302
IOI cracked
the first three lines of the clue,

1194
01:17:19,469 --> 01:17:20,512
so they knew it was sector 14

1195
01:17:20,678 --> 01:17:22,472
but they couldn't figure out
"the fortress tragic."

1196
01:17:22,639 --> 01:17:24,974
So they sent every guide
they had into that sector

1197
01:17:25,141 --> 01:17:27,018
until they found the right fortress.

1198
01:17:28,144 --> 01:17:29,437
Sho?

1199
01:17:29,604 --> 01:17:31,731
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I'm 11, so what?

1200
01:17:31,898 --> 01:17:33,775
His real name is Xo.

1201
01:17:33,942 --> 01:17:36,528
But everyone else calls me Sho,
no big deal.

1202
01:17:36,694 --> 01:17:39,322
No. It is a big deal.

1203
01:17:39,489 --> 01:17:42,909
Sho, you're the world's most badass
11 -year-old ever.

1204
01:17:43,034 --> 01:17:44,035
He knows.

1205
01:17:44,118 --> 01:17:46,162
Shut up! Let him tell me.

1206
01:17:46,329 --> 01:17:47,372
Aech!

1207
01:17:50,917 --> 01:17:52,460
We have to go save Samantha.

1208
01:17:52,627 --> 01:17:54,838
Well, we can't just
go through the doors of IOI.

1209
01:17:55,004 --> 01:17:57,048
Look, I've been thinkin' about it.
I got a better plan.

1210
01:17:57,215 --> 01:17:59,050
You saw Sorrento's rig, right?

1211
01:17:59,217 --> 01:18:00,218
Yeah.

1212
01:18:00,385 --> 01:18:03,596
Let's go after the man himself and
make him give Art3mis back to us.

1213
01:18:03,763 --> 01:18:05,515
But first, I have to know exactly,

1214
01:18:05,682 --> 01:18:07,600
how much about Sorrento's rig
do you remember?

1215
01:18:09,060 --> 01:18:11,312
Kind of everything.

1216
01:18:25,076 --> 01:18:28,913
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Maintenance,
report to loyalty pod 31-B.</i>

1217
01:18:33,042 --> 01:18:37,589
<i>Security, please report
to section 97 for escort.</i>

1218
01:18:53,062 --> 01:18:54,480
(GRUNTING)

1219
01:18:58,401 --> 01:19:01,195
Hey! Newbie, get to work.

1220
01:19:03,406 --> 01:19:04,741
Get to work.

1221
01:19:07,785 --> 01:19:09,454
(GROANING)

1222
01:19:10,830 --> 01:19:13,917
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Work violation.
Work violation.</i>

1223
01:19:15,710 --> 01:19:18,755
Lay those charges every six feet.

1224
01:19:21,883 --> 01:19:23,092
(GRUNTS)

1225
01:19:23,801 --> 01:19:25,929
Keep it moving!

1226
01:19:27,263 --> 01:19:28,264
Hey, you!

1227
01:19:30,433 --> 01:19:32,185
Those are explosives!

1228
01:19:32,268 --> 01:19:33,519
(GROANING)

1229
01:19:33,645 --> 01:19:37,023
IOI will not reimburse any lost coin
if you zero out.

1230
01:19:37,190 --> 01:19:38,942
Keep it moving!

1231
01:19:43,696 --> 01:19:46,574
So what is this challenge,
some sort of video game thing?

1232
01:19:46,741 --> 01:19:48,660
An Atari 2600, sir.

1233
01:19:48,826 --> 01:19:52,372
And every game ever made for it,
thousands of possibilities.

1234
01:19:53,206 --> 01:19:54,207
MAN: Come up!

1235
01:19:54,582 --> 01:19:55,750
(SCREAMS)

1236
01:19:56,834 --> 01:19:58,044
(NOLAN SNICKERING)

1237
01:19:59,045 --> 01:20:00,338
Halliday,

1238
01:20:00,505 --> 01:20:01,881
this is how you plan to resolve

1239
01:20:02,048 --> 01:20:05,093
the fate of the world's
most important economic resource?

1240
01:20:05,885 --> 01:20:07,679
- Call me when you're close.
- Yes, sir.

1241
01:20:07,845 --> 01:20:09,389
Go, go! No! Ahh!

1242
01:20:11,641 --> 01:20:14,519
One minute into <i>Centipede,</i>
the ice broke.

1243
01:20:14,936 --> 01:20:16,437
It has to be <i>Joust!</i>

1244
01:20:16,562 --> 01:20:19,732
Halliday still holds the world record
on the 2600 port of that game.

1245
01:20:19,899 --> 01:20:21,317
Maybe we just need
to beat his high score.

1246
01:20:21,484 --> 01:20:24,028
<i>Pitfall!</i> One of the only 2600 games
that still hasn't ended.

1247
01:20:24,195 --> 01:20:25,321
MAN 1: And how about
those <i>Swordquest</i> games?

1248
01:20:25,488 --> 01:20:26,531
MAN 2: Yes! The <i>Swordquest</i> games.

1249
01:20:26,698 --> 01:20:29,534
They were created
for a contest Atari held with real...

1250
01:20:37,291 --> 01:20:38,918
I-R0k, how are we doin'?

1251
01:20:40,294 --> 01:20:42,380
To be honest, I think I need
physical therapy because it's not...

1252
01:20:42,547 --> 01:20:44,549
Is the Orb ready?

1253
01:20:45,550 --> 01:20:47,218
Um, as you wish.

1254
01:20:49,053 --> 01:20:50,513
(GRUNTING)

1255
01:20:51,389 --> 01:20:52,390
The Orb...

1256
01:20:52,557 --> 01:20:53,975
Of Osuvox.

1257
01:20:54,851 --> 01:20:55,935
Ah...

1258
01:20:56,019 --> 01:20:57,395
How does it work?

1259
01:20:57,562 --> 01:21:01,357
Has it got, like, a remote
or is there a button or something?

1260
01:21:01,524 --> 01:21:04,986
Nolan, it's a level-99 magic artifact,

1261
01:21:05,153 --> 01:21:08,781
not one of your drones,
so it is activated by a magic spell.

1262
01:21:08,948 --> 01:21:10,992
Would you care to do the honors?

1263
01:21:21,335 --> 01:21:23,588
(CHANTING IN OTHER LANGUAGE)

1264
01:22:01,209 --> 01:22:02,251
(GUNS COCKING)

1265
01:22:02,960 --> 01:22:04,170
WADE: Where is she?

1266
01:22:04,337 --> 01:22:05,463
How'd you get in here?

1267
01:22:05,630 --> 01:22:06,756
- Art3mis.
- Who?

1268
01:22:06,923 --> 01:22:09,967
Samantha Cook. Where is she?

1269
01:22:11,594 --> 01:22:14,972
If you wanna talk, we can talk,
but you gotta put that gun down.

1270
01:22:15,473 --> 01:22:17,809
You killed my mom's sister.

1271
01:22:18,392 --> 01:22:19,894
You think I won't kill you?

1272
01:22:20,019 --> 01:22:24,065
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Just slow down, okay?

1273
01:22:24,232 --> 01:22:27,443
That was a corporate decision.
It was not personal.

1274
01:22:27,610 --> 01:22:28,611
Where is she?

1275
01:22:28,778 --> 01:22:31,114
She's downstairs in the loyalty center!

1276
01:22:31,280 --> 01:22:34,033
I know
she's in the goddamn loyalty center.

1277
01:22:34,617 --> 01:22:36,911
You're gonna tell me
exactly which rig she's in

1278
01:22:37,078 --> 01:22:39,413
and the access code to contact her.

1279
01:22:40,498 --> 01:22:42,750
Yeah, that seems appropriate.

1280
01:22:45,628 --> 01:22:47,630
TOSHIRO: Start with access code.

1281
01:22:48,840 --> 01:22:50,967
NOLAN: 6, 45, 7, 25.

1282
01:22:51,134 --> 01:22:52,385
TOSHIRO: Where's the rig?

1283
01:23:03,312 --> 01:23:04,897
I think he pissed himself.

1284
01:23:05,523 --> 01:23:07,358
Good job, Z. We're in his account.

1285
01:23:07,525 --> 01:23:09,277
So he really doesn't know
he's in the OASIS?

1286
01:23:11,654 --> 01:23:14,073
This is what Sorrento should be seeing,

1287
01:23:14,240 --> 01:23:17,368
but this... This is what we're
making him see.

1288
01:23:18,494 --> 01:23:21,372
We grabbed him in transit just
as he was logging out of the OASIS,

1289
01:23:21,539 --> 01:23:24,208
so he thinks he's back in his office
in the real world.

1290
01:23:24,417 --> 01:23:28,087
But actually, he's here,
in the identical office that Aech built.

1291
01:23:28,254 --> 01:23:30,798
SHO: So, you basically
just remotely hacked his rig.

1292
01:23:30,965 --> 01:23:33,843
AECH: A fixed rig like Sorrento's
is easy to locate, hard to hack.

1293
01:23:34,010 --> 01:23:36,554
WADE: Unless he's stupid enough
to leave his password lying around.

1294
01:23:36,721 --> 01:23:37,972
AECH: Loyalty center, I'm in.

1295
01:23:38,139 --> 01:23:39,891
WADE: All right, let's get to work.

1296
01:23:47,690 --> 01:23:49,859
- WADE: <i>Arty.</i>
- Z? Z? Z?

1297
01:23:50,026 --> 01:23:51,402
Arty, don't say anything.

1298
01:23:51,569 --> 01:23:53,529
I'm tapped directly
into your audio feed.

1299
01:23:55,156 --> 01:23:56,240
ART3MIS: <i>How did you find me?</i>

1300
01:23:56,407 --> 01:23:58,367
We got his password,
hacked Sorrento's rig.

1301
01:23:59,994 --> 01:24:01,746
Z, I have something to tell you.

1302
01:24:02,038 --> 01:24:04,290
<i>Not now. I have something to show you
that'll get you out of there.</i>

1303
01:24:04,457 --> 01:24:07,043
The Sixers found the third challenge.
It's on Planet Doom.

1304
01:24:07,919 --> 01:24:09,295
And there's more,
they just put a force field

1305
01:24:09,462 --> 01:24:11,255
around Anorak's Castle.

1306
01:24:15,718 --> 01:24:18,221
I heard one of the guards calling it
"the Orb of Osuvox,"

1307
01:24:18,387 --> 01:24:20,765
and the only way to take it down
is from the inside.

1308
01:24:20,932 --> 01:24:23,935
She's right. Level-99 artifact,

1309
01:24:24,101 --> 01:24:26,896
creates a magic-resistant,
impenetrable barrier.

1310
01:24:27,063 --> 01:24:28,064
No way through it.

1311
01:24:28,231 --> 01:24:29,649
Okay, listen.
That's not important right now.

1312
01:24:29,815 --> 01:24:31,859
What's important is
that we get you out of the rig.

1313
01:24:34,654 --> 01:24:36,948
<i>All right, so I'm looking at a diagram
of your rig.</i>

1314
01:24:39,700 --> 01:24:41,953
If you reach up with your left hand
at 11 o'clock,

1315
01:24:42,119 --> 01:24:43,913
there's a panel above your head.

1316
01:24:48,709 --> 01:24:50,711
Yeah, yeah. Yeah, I can feel it.

1317
01:24:50,878 --> 01:24:52,672
WADE: <i>Okay, there should be
two release handles.</i>

1318
01:24:52,838 --> 01:24:54,257
<i>Nine o'clock and three o'clock.
Can you feel them?</i>

1319
01:24:54,423 --> 01:24:56,759
- Yeah, I got it.
<i>- Okay, pull it towards you.</i>

1320
01:24:57,510 --> 01:24:58,636
(GRUNTS)

1321
01:24:59,136 --> 01:25:00,638
<i>Okay, inside the panel, there's a lever.</i>

1322
01:25:00,805 --> 01:25:03,266
<i>Grab it with your right hand
and slide it to the left.</i>

1323
01:25:03,432 --> 01:25:04,850
<i>That should release you.</i>

1324
01:25:04,934 --> 01:25:06,018
(GRUNTS)

1325
01:25:09,814 --> 01:25:12,108
- (BEEPING)
- (EXHALES)

1326
01:25:12,191 --> 01:25:13,985
It worked. It worked, I'm out.

1327
01:25:14,944 --> 01:25:16,988
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Loyalty pod 41-F,</i>

1328
01:25:17,071 --> 01:25:19,991
<i>you are on an authorized
break for 10 minutes.</i>

1329
01:25:25,329 --> 01:25:28,332
<i>Pod 41-F, you are on 10-minute break.</i>

1330
01:25:28,499 --> 01:25:30,626
<i>Proceed to break area.</i>

1331
01:25:31,919 --> 01:25:33,129
Wade, are you still there?

1332
01:25:33,296 --> 01:25:34,338
<i>Yeah, I'm here. Where are you?</i>

1333
01:25:34,505 --> 01:25:35,589
Where is Sorrento's office?

1334
01:25:35,756 --> 01:25:37,967
<i>It's in the IOI war room,
two levels above where you are now.</i>

1335
01:25:38,134 --> 01:25:39,760
<i>But that's not the way out.</i>

1336
01:25:39,927 --> 01:25:41,470
What's his password?

1337
01:25:42,805 --> 01:25:43,931
Wade, answer me.

1338
01:25:44,098 --> 01:25:47,977
<i>Okay, it's capital B-0-55-man-69.</i>

1339
01:25:48,144 --> 01:25:50,354
<i>But, Arty, you need to go.</i>

1340
01:25:50,521 --> 01:25:51,814
You need to raise an army.

1341
01:25:52,732 --> 01:25:53,733
An army?

1342
01:25:53,899 --> 01:25:55,901
<i>Get to Planet Doom,
and wait for my signal.</i>

1343
01:25:55,985 --> 01:25:56,986
What signal?

1344
01:25:57,278 --> 01:25:58,487
I'm gonna take down that shield.

1345
01:25:58,654 --> 01:26:01,073
<i>Wait, Arty, wait!
You gotta get out of there! Arty!</i>

1346
01:26:09,749 --> 01:26:12,209
Hey, how much are they paying you?

1347
01:26:12,376 --> 01:26:14,003
- 'Cause, man, I got a lot of paper.
- (TOSHIRO SHUSHING)

1348
01:26:14,170 --> 01:26:16,380
You know, I can make you,
like, a forest.

1349
01:26:16,547 --> 01:26:18,674
Hey, shut up.

1350
01:26:18,841 --> 01:26:19,925
Okay.

1351
01:26:42,573 --> 01:26:44,742
This isn't real, you're tapping my feed.

1352
01:26:44,825 --> 01:26:46,827
Uh-oh. Guys.

1353
01:27:05,388 --> 01:27:07,932
F'Nale, they've hacked my rig.
They're after the girl.

1354
01:27:08,099 --> 01:27:09,767
Meet me at loyalty.

1355
01:27:10,393 --> 01:27:12,561
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

1356
01:27:23,906 --> 01:27:27,326
AUTOMATED VOICE: <i>Pod 41-F,
you have exceeded your break time.</i>

1357
01:27:27,493 --> 01:27:31,205
<i>Report to security or your coin count
will be reset to zero.</i>

1358
01:27:40,172 --> 01:27:44,802
So, she just walks out of here,
how does that happen?

1359
01:27:44,969 --> 01:27:47,012
They're smart.
They knew what they were doing.

1360
01:27:47,179 --> 01:27:49,932
But we know they're in Columbus.
And now, all five of them are together.

1361
01:27:50,099 --> 01:27:52,435
Wait. Wait, we know what?
How do we know?

1362
01:27:52,601 --> 01:27:56,188
We have the make and model of the van.
We'll spot them.

1363
01:27:56,355 --> 01:27:58,315
"We'll spot them"?

1364
01:27:58,482 --> 01:28:01,569
That sounds like a great inscription
for our tombstones.

1365
01:28:01,735 --> 01:28:03,112
Why didn't you tell me this earlier?

1366
01:28:03,279 --> 01:28:04,697
It wasn't relevant yet.

1367
01:28:04,864 --> 01:28:05,948
I need to know where they are.

1368
01:28:06,115 --> 01:28:07,491
We need to know. We need to find them!

1369
01:28:07,658 --> 01:28:10,536
They're kids, Nolan. Man the hell up!

1370
01:28:10,703 --> 01:28:13,747
Do your job, and I'll do mine,
unless you wanna take this

1371
01:28:13,914 --> 01:28:15,916
and go after them yourself.

1372
01:28:20,504 --> 01:28:21,755
Find them!

1373
01:28:30,764 --> 01:28:35,352
<i>The Complete Nancy Drew,</i>
Kegel Exercises for...

1374
01:28:37,021 --> 01:28:39,190
Bingo. Okay.

1375
01:28:39,773 --> 01:28:41,859
"Congratulations, you are
the proud owner of the Orb of Osuvox,

1376
01:28:42,026 --> 01:28:43,360
"a 99th level magic artifact.

1377
01:28:43,527 --> 01:28:46,655
"Read these instructions
before deploying. To turn orb on, off."

1378
01:28:46,822 --> 01:28:48,157
Off! Yes, off.

1379
01:28:48,324 --> 01:28:50,576
"Utter spell within 10 feet of orb."

1380
01:28:52,328 --> 01:28:56,457
(CHANTING IN OTHER LANGUAGE)

1381
01:29:04,548 --> 01:29:06,592
Citizens of the OASIS,

1382
01:29:06,759 --> 01:29:09,053
I am Parzival, first to the key.

1383
01:29:09,595 --> 01:29:12,473
I'm here talking to all of you now
because our future's being threatened

1384
01:29:12,640 --> 01:29:15,726
by people who will stop at nothing
to win this contest.

1385
01:29:16,727 --> 01:29:18,479
Some of you already know this,

1386
01:29:18,646 --> 01:29:21,941
and you've lost much more
than just your avatars or your weapons.

1387
01:29:22,733 --> 01:29:26,612
Some have lost their freedom.
Some have lost their lives.

1388
01:29:29,114 --> 01:29:31,075
And now, this.

1389
01:29:31,909 --> 01:29:34,870
<i>A force field
around the third challenge.</i>

1390
01:29:37,414 --> 01:29:40,543
<i>I only came here to escape
the shitty hand that life dealt me.</i>

1391
01:29:41,418 --> 01:29:44,046
<i>But I stayed, like many of you,</i>

1392
01:29:44,213 --> 01:29:48,842
<i>because I found something
much bigger than just myself.</i>

1393
01:29:49,301 --> 01:29:51,095
<i>I found a cause.</i>

1394
01:29:52,263 --> 01:29:54,348
<i>I found my friends.</i>

1395
01:29:55,558 --> 01:29:58,978
And yes, I know
it's kind of a groaner, but...

1396
01:30:00,312 --> 01:30:01,897
<i>I found love.</i>

1397
01:30:03,190 --> 01:30:04,483
<i>And I don't wanna lose that</i>

1398
01:30:04,650 --> 01:30:07,319
<i>to this colossal douchebag,
Nolan Sorrento.</i>

1399
01:30:07,486 --> 01:30:10,948
This guy. Back to work, people.

1400
01:30:11,699 --> 01:30:14,535
<i>He thinks that we're all
too distracted to even notice...</i>

1401
01:30:15,953 --> 01:30:20,583
<i>Nolan Sorrento thinks
that we won't put up a fight.</i>

1402
01:30:20,749 --> 01:30:21,917
Sir! Sir!

1403
01:30:22,001 --> 01:30:23,002
This is going out live!

1404
01:30:23,085 --> 01:30:24,169
WADE: <i>The only thing</i>
<i>Halliday let this guy</i> do...

1405
01:30:24,336 --> 01:30:26,589
- It's absolutely everywhere.
<i>- ...was get him a cup of coffee.</i>

1406
01:30:26,755 --> 01:30:28,424
<i>And now, we're supposed
to hand him the OASIS?</i>

1407
01:30:36,348 --> 01:30:39,101
NOLAN: This Parzival... Oh, man.

1408
01:30:43,188 --> 01:30:45,524
Come on, come on. Give me this thing.

1409
01:30:45,691 --> 01:30:46,817
MAN: Yes, sir.

1410
01:30:47,526 --> 01:30:49,486
NOLAN: Left arm.

1411
01:30:49,653 --> 01:30:51,989
- Left arm!
- MAN: Sir.

1412
01:30:52,156 --> 01:30:53,991
NOLAN: No, I need the left arm.

1413
01:30:54,158 --> 01:30:56,452
No, I don't care if... I want it on.

1414
01:30:58,579 --> 01:31:01,040
WADE: He thinks
that we won't even put up a fight!

1415
01:31:01,123 --> 01:31:03,751
Well, I say he's wrong.

1416
01:31:03,917 --> 01:31:07,546
I say, tell that to the gunter clans
in the gold mines of Gygax.

1417
01:31:07,713 --> 01:31:10,883
(WHISPERING)
Activate the Iron Giant.

1418
01:31:17,348 --> 01:31:18,432
(GRUNTING)

1419
01:31:35,032 --> 01:31:39,953
Ask yourselves, are you willing
to zero out for the OASIS?

1420
01:31:40,120 --> 01:31:41,997
Are you willing to fight?

1421
01:31:43,457 --> 01:31:45,876
I am Parzival of the High Five.

1422
01:31:46,043 --> 01:31:48,629
In the name of Art3mis,
in the name of Aech,

1423
01:31:48,796 --> 01:31:50,923
in the name of Daito and Sho,

1424
01:31:51,507 --> 01:31:54,051
we ask you to join us on Planet Doom.

1425
01:31:55,052 --> 01:31:58,013
In the name of James Halliday himself,

1426
01:31:58,180 --> 01:32:00,182
help us save the OASIS.

1427
01:32:05,062 --> 01:32:07,064
(WIND HOWLING)

1428
01:32:23,914 --> 01:32:26,667
(DISTANT RUMBLING)

1429
01:32:32,631 --> 01:32:35,801
(RUMBLING INTENSIFIES)

1430
01:32:40,389 --> 01:32:42,558
(PEOPLE SHOUTING)

1431
01:32:55,195 --> 01:32:57,573
No, no, no, no.

1432
01:33:07,708 --> 01:33:10,252
"No man is a failure who has friends."

1433
01:33:10,335 --> 01:33:11,545
(NOLAN GROWLS)

1434
01:33:32,441 --> 01:33:35,611
SOLDIER: <i>Squadron 14, armor up,
you're in the lead.</i>

1435
01:33:46,163 --> 01:33:47,581
(GRUNTS)

1436
01:33:48,540 --> 01:33:51,251
One minute into <i>Swordquest,</i>
the ice broke.

1437
01:33:52,961 --> 01:33:56,548
(SIGHS) Well, all three <i>Swordquests.</i>
What's next?

1438
01:33:56,715 --> 01:33:58,383
(OVERLAPPING)
<i>Dark Cavern, Laser Blast.</i>

1439
01:33:58,550 --> 01:33:59,635
It's <i>Adventure.</i>

1440
01:33:59,802 --> 01:34:01,887
Released in 1979, for the 2600,

1441
01:34:02,054 --> 01:34:03,597
<i>Adventure</i> was created by
Warren Robinett,

1442
01:34:03,764 --> 01:34:06,141
who was the first video game designer
ever to hide his name. In fact...

1443
01:34:06,308 --> 01:34:08,310
- (CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)
- Try <i>Adventure.</i>

1444
01:34:09,561 --> 01:34:11,063
Play <i>Adventure.</i>

1445
01:34:16,902 --> 01:34:18,320
(PANTING)

1446
01:34:18,403 --> 01:34:20,155
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

1447
01:34:33,794 --> 01:34:35,921
(CONTINUES PANTING)

1448
01:34:39,091 --> 01:34:40,092
(DEVICE TRILLING)

1449
01:35:03,448 --> 01:35:05,617
More than a minute, we're still alive.

1450
01:35:05,784 --> 01:35:07,578
This must be the right game.

1451
01:35:07,828 --> 01:35:10,873
(ART3MIS CHANTING IN OTHER LANGUAGE)

1452
01:35:14,585 --> 01:35:17,379
How long does it last, this orb thing?

1453
01:35:20,674 --> 01:35:23,343
(CHANTING IN OTHER LANGUAGE)

1454
01:35:24,845 --> 01:35:27,431
I'd say about ten...

1455
01:35:27,598 --> 01:35:30,684
Yeah, about 10 million years,
so we should be fine.

1456
01:35:30,976 --> 01:35:34,021
(CHANTING IN OTHER LANGUAGE)

1457
01:35:48,160 --> 01:35:49,870
First to the key!

1458
01:35:50,037 --> 01:35:51,705
ALL: First to the egg!

1459
01:35:51,872 --> 01:35:53,206
First to the egg!

1460
01:35:53,290 --> 01:35:54,541
First to the egg!

1461
01:35:54,750 --> 01:35:56,043
(1980s ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

1462
01:36:23,070 --> 01:36:24,154
<i>Adventure.</i>

1463
01:36:33,372 --> 01:36:35,499
- (SQUEALING)
- (ALL GRUNTING)

1464
01:36:38,085 --> 01:36:39,711
(MAN YELLING)

1465
01:36:40,587 --> 01:36:42,798
- (GRUNTS)
- MAN: What? Come on!

1466
01:36:44,466 --> 01:36:45,759
- (GRUNTS)
- (GROANS)

1467
01:36:59,982 --> 01:37:01,900
(GRUNTING)

1468
01:37:09,116 --> 01:37:11,201
- (BEEPING)
- (MAN GROANS)

1469
01:37:12,411 --> 01:37:13,996
WADE: Whoa, whoa, whoa!

1470
01:37:16,164 --> 01:37:18,750
The Sixers are in the final challenge.
It's an Atari 2600.

1471
01:37:18,917 --> 01:37:20,627
Are you in the Sixer war room?

1472
01:37:21,169 --> 01:37:22,587
No, no, no. You gotta get out of there.

1473
01:37:22,754 --> 01:37:24,423
They're playing <i>Adventure.</i>

1474
01:37:25,048 --> 01:37:27,300
<i>Adventure,</i> of course!

1475
01:37:27,467 --> 01:37:28,927
Created by Warren Robinett!

1476
01:37:29,094 --> 01:37:30,637
He was the first designer
to ever hide an Easter egg in...

1477
01:37:30,804 --> 01:37:31,805
Dude!

1478
01:37:36,852 --> 01:37:39,521
We're looking for a USPS truck,
Ohio plates,

1479
01:37:39,688 --> 01:37:42,691
a drone spitter, 2036 model.

1480
01:38:01,251 --> 01:38:04,588
Daito! When are you
getting into this fight?

1481
01:38:17,142 --> 01:38:18,226
(GUN CLICKING)

1482
01:38:18,310 --> 01:38:19,686
- I'm out. Inventory's empty.
- (ALARM BEEPING)

1483
01:38:19,853 --> 01:38:20,854
Last clip for me.

1484
01:38:21,021 --> 01:38:22,064
More weapons!

1485
01:38:22,230 --> 01:38:24,232
Anti-personnel ordinance cannon!

1486
01:38:24,399 --> 01:38:26,318
Anti-personnel ordinance cannon!

1487
01:38:27,652 --> 01:38:28,904
(ALL GROAN)

1488
01:38:29,279 --> 01:38:30,572
Railgun!

1489
01:38:30,739 --> 01:38:31,948
Railgun!

1490
01:38:33,158 --> 01:38:34,242
(ALL GROAN)

1491
01:38:37,162 --> 01:38:38,330
Yo, Z!

1492
01:38:38,872 --> 01:38:42,501
Yo, Z! Try this little guy.

1493
01:38:43,335 --> 01:38:44,711
(LAUGHING EVILLY)

1494
01:38:44,795 --> 01:38:46,004
(WADE YELPING)

1495
01:38:46,088 --> 01:38:47,255
- (SCREAMS)
- CHUCKY: Ow!

1496
01:38:47,756 --> 01:38:49,591
Get rid of it! Get rid of it!

1497
01:38:50,717 --> 01:38:52,511
It's fucking Chucky!

1498
01:38:52,594 --> 01:38:54,262
(CHUCKY LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

1499
01:38:55,180 --> 01:38:57,766
(ALL GROANING)

1500
01:38:57,849 --> 01:38:59,351
COMMANDER: Move! Move!

1501
01:38:59,935 --> 01:39:01,436
Go, go, go!

1502
01:39:18,829 --> 01:39:20,622
(ALL YELLING)

1503
01:39:59,202 --> 01:40:00,704
Mechagodzilla!

1504
01:40:00,787 --> 01:40:03,165
(ROARING)

1505
01:40:20,182 --> 01:40:21,600
(SCREAMING)

1506
01:40:21,892 --> 01:40:25,228
WADE: Daito, we need you! Daito, now!

1507
01:40:25,395 --> 01:40:27,564
Get to the bridge.
Go now, he's distracted.

1508
01:40:27,647 --> 01:40:28,648
Go, go, go.

1509
01:40:36,615 --> 01:40:38,491
(ROARS)

1510
01:40:44,873 --> 01:40:46,374
(SPEAKING JAPANESE)

1511
01:41:08,104 --> 01:41:09,856
(BOTH YELPING)

1512
01:41:09,981 --> 01:41:10,982
Z!

1513
01:41:12,108 --> 01:41:13,401
(ART3MIS SCREAMS)

1514
01:41:18,406 --> 01:41:19,574
(SCREAMS)

1515
01:41:21,660 --> 01:41:23,787
(ALL GROANING)

1516
01:41:27,791 --> 01:41:29,501
(AECH GROANS)

1517
01:41:30,919 --> 01:41:31,920
Arty!

1518
01:41:32,003 --> 01:41:34,256
Get to the castle!
Win the third key before they do!

1519
01:41:42,305 --> 01:41:43,556
(ROARS)

1520
01:41:43,682 --> 01:41:45,934
(ALARM BEEPING)

1521
01:41:46,017 --> 01:41:47,227
What is that?

1522
01:41:47,394 --> 01:41:50,105
SHO: He's only got 30 seconds
before changing back!

1523
01:41:55,610 --> 01:41:57,570
(ALARM CONTINUES BEEPING)

1524
01:42:01,324 --> 01:42:04,202
Daito, abort, abort! You got 10 seconds!

1525
01:42:07,038 --> 01:42:08,498
(ALARM TRILLS)

1526
01:42:09,666 --> 01:42:11,960
(ALARM BEEPING RAPIDLY)

1527
01:42:18,883 --> 01:42:20,093
DAITO: First to the egg!

1528
01:42:23,763 --> 01:42:25,557
- (ROARING)
- (WADE AND SHO SCREAM)

1529
01:42:30,812 --> 01:42:32,105
(MISSILES ARMING)

1530
01:42:37,193 --> 01:42:39,404
(AECH GRUNTING)

1531
01:42:59,549 --> 01:43:00,842
Shit, it's her.

1532
01:43:04,471 --> 01:43:05,764
(OBJECT GIGGLES)

1533
01:43:08,725 --> 01:43:10,268
(CACKLING)

1534
01:43:20,904 --> 01:43:23,448
WADE: Arty! Arty!

1535
01:43:24,240 --> 01:43:26,451
SHO: Z! Got to get to the castle!

1536
01:43:26,951 --> 01:43:29,037
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

1537
01:43:32,791 --> 01:43:35,377
She never left. She's still here.

1538
01:43:38,338 --> 01:43:39,839
The girl's in the war room.

1539
01:43:39,923 --> 01:43:41,758
(ALARM TICKING)

1540
01:43:52,352 --> 01:43:54,396
(PEOPLE CLAMORING)

1541
01:44:18,002 --> 01:44:19,546
No, no, no.

1542
01:44:27,846 --> 01:44:28,847
(GROANING)

1543
01:44:33,685 --> 01:44:36,229
- (AECH GRUNTS)
- WADE: Sho! Hang on!

1544
01:44:43,820 --> 01:44:45,530
(ALARM BEEPING)

1545
01:44:49,367 --> 01:44:50,368
(SHO GRUNTS)

1546
01:44:55,665 --> 01:44:57,250
No!

1547
01:45:01,171 --> 01:45:02,755
(GRUNTING)

1548
01:45:19,731 --> 01:45:21,232
WADE: Arty, we've got this.
You need to log out.

1549
01:45:21,649 --> 01:45:24,235
If the game is <i>Adventure,</i>
why haven't they won yet?

1550
01:45:24,402 --> 01:45:26,112
I don't know. Arty, Arty.

1551
01:45:26,279 --> 01:45:28,198
I'm serious, Sorrento's crazy.
He'll kill you.

1552
01:45:30,450 --> 01:45:31,910
<i>What are you looking at?</i>

1553
01:45:32,410 --> 01:45:34,162
There's nothing over there.

1554
01:45:35,205 --> 01:45:36,206
You're in trouble, aren't you?

1555
01:45:39,667 --> 01:45:43,046
Samantha, you know I love you.

1556
01:45:43,213 --> 01:45:44,422
Not the time, Z.

1557
01:45:44,589 --> 01:45:45,882
I can handle the challenge,

1558
01:45:46,049 --> 01:45:47,884
but I can't let you get hurt
in the real world.

1559
01:45:49,135 --> 01:45:52,305
Get out of IOI,
and meet us at River South.

1560
01:45:58,686 --> 01:46:00,230
Wade, no.

1561
01:46:00,396 --> 01:46:02,106
You'll forgive me for this, I promise.

1562
01:46:02,273 --> 01:46:03,399
Wade, no, no, no.

1563
01:46:04,359 --> 01:46:05,443
(GRUNTS)

1564
01:46:05,568 --> 01:46:06,819
(ALARM BEEPS)

1565
01:46:13,535 --> 01:46:16,538
Get it together, Sixer. Back to respawn.

1566
01:46:16,996 --> 01:46:18,164
Let's go, move.

1567
01:46:18,331 --> 01:46:19,541
You're in.

1568
01:46:37,809 --> 01:46:40,270
Holy hand grenade!
How much did that cost?

1569
01:46:40,436 --> 01:46:42,897
Less than it's gonna cost them.

1570
01:46:44,023 --> 01:46:45,525
What is that?

1571
01:46:55,910 --> 01:46:58,454
Sir, the gunters are approaching
the challenge.

1572
01:46:58,621 --> 01:47:00,498
- I-R0k?
- In position, sir.

1573
01:47:00,623 --> 01:47:01,624
Prepare my rig.

1574
01:47:01,916 --> 01:47:04,544
The ice is holding. Still going.

1575
01:47:14,887 --> 01:47:16,055
WADE: Wait.

1576
01:47:16,222 --> 01:47:17,348
He's trying to win.

1577
01:47:20,727 --> 01:47:23,271
Yeah! I won.

1578
01:47:26,774 --> 01:47:28,568
He lost.

1579
01:47:28,735 --> 01:47:30,737
Not <i>Adventure.</i>

1580
01:47:32,113 --> 01:47:33,615
(ALL CLAMORING)

1581
01:47:34,866 --> 01:47:39,162
Everyone who wins loses.

1582
01:47:39,329 --> 01:47:42,624
It's not about winning.
It's about playing.

1583
01:47:43,750 --> 01:47:45,793
Remember Halliday's announcement.

1584
01:47:46,252 --> 01:47:48,504
The keys are invisible,
and they're hidden in a dark room

1585
01:47:48,671 --> 01:47:50,632
that's at the center of a maze.

1586
01:47:51,257 --> 01:47:54,761
Well, there's a secret in <i>Adventure,</i>
and you don't find it by winning.

1587
01:47:54,927 --> 01:47:57,347
You find it
by wandering around in a dark room.

1588
01:47:57,847 --> 01:47:59,390
Until you get to the invisible dot.

1589
01:47:59,557 --> 01:48:01,100
It's pretty easy
if you know what you're doing.

1590
01:48:01,267 --> 01:48:02,518
NOLAN: Really?

1591
01:48:03,436 --> 01:48:05,480
Let me finish it for you.

1592
01:48:05,813 --> 01:48:07,148
(SHO GRUNTING)

1593
01:48:09,776 --> 01:48:11,027
It's your last chance, Wade.

1594
01:48:11,694 --> 01:48:14,447
Last chance. Give me the key.

1595
01:48:14,614 --> 01:48:18,701
I give you 50 million
in your account right now.

1596
01:48:19,661 --> 01:48:21,412
Why the hell would I ever do that?

1597
01:48:23,206 --> 01:48:24,874
SHO: Dude! That's the Cataclyst.

1598
01:48:25,166 --> 01:48:26,876
Now, personally, I don't care.

1599
01:48:27,043 --> 01:48:28,628
I'd just as soon
never set foot in the OASIS again,

1600
01:48:28,795 --> 01:48:30,797
let alone have to deal
with any of this absurdity.

1601
01:48:30,963 --> 01:48:34,258
But I know how important
Halliday's competition is to you, so...

1602
01:48:36,177 --> 01:48:40,431
I will never let the future of the OASIS
rest in your hands, Nolan Sorrento.

1603
01:48:40,598 --> 01:48:44,477
Well, that's fine.
Three easy steps. One.

1604
01:48:44,644 --> 01:48:46,938
Wait, I thought you were bluffing.
You know that kills all of us, right?

1605
01:48:47,105 --> 01:48:49,023
I've got 10 years' worth of shit
inside of me.

1606
01:48:49,190 --> 01:48:50,692
Last chance. Two.

1607
01:48:50,858 --> 01:48:52,068
I'm not goin' out like that.

1608
01:48:52,235 --> 01:48:53,319
That's a camper move.

1609
01:48:53,486 --> 01:48:54,654
You don't even know
how to activate an orb.

1610
01:48:54,904 --> 01:48:56,197
(WADE GRUNTS)

1611
01:48:59,701 --> 01:49:01,077
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1612
01:49:05,123 --> 01:49:06,249
(PANTING)

1613
01:49:07,083 --> 01:49:08,167
Yeah, I felt those.

1614
01:49:09,585 --> 01:49:11,671
But this is my world, Sorrento.

1615
01:49:15,633 --> 01:49:16,884
Hadouken!

1616
01:49:18,386 --> 01:49:19,887
(GRUNTS)

1617
01:49:22,473 --> 01:49:23,558
(GROANS)

1618
01:49:26,185 --> 01:49:27,478
(GROANS)

1619
01:49:36,487 --> 01:49:38,948
- No, no, no!
- Step three.

1620
01:49:39,115 --> 01:49:40,825
No, no, no!

1621
01:49:43,161 --> 01:49:44,579
(WHIMPERS)

1622
01:49:48,791 --> 01:49:50,251
(YELPING)

1623
01:50:07,560 --> 01:50:09,020
(PLAYERS GROANING)

1624
01:50:38,341 --> 01:50:40,009
Get me out of this thing.

1625
01:50:54,482 --> 01:50:55,817
Uh...

1626
01:50:55,900 --> 01:50:57,151
Guys?

1627
01:51:03,741 --> 01:51:05,576
Z. He's still alive!

1628
01:51:13,501 --> 01:51:15,294
Extra life.

1629
01:51:17,713 --> 01:51:19,131
Thanks, Curator.

1630
01:51:22,009 --> 01:51:23,135
Hold on.

1631
01:51:30,893 --> 01:51:32,895
Live feed in all OASIS channels.

1632
01:51:33,521 --> 01:51:35,940
Halliday's letting everyone
watch the end of the contest.

1633
01:51:36,107 --> 01:51:37,316
(LAUGHS) That's so Halliday.

1634
01:51:37,483 --> 01:51:39,569
God damn it, we tried <i>Adventure.</i>

1635
01:51:39,735 --> 01:51:41,028
No, we tried to win it.

1636
01:51:41,195 --> 01:51:43,614
But the hidden room isn't
at the end of the game.

1637
01:51:43,781 --> 01:51:46,534
You've gotta go straight
to the invisible dot at the start.

1638
01:51:52,874 --> 01:51:54,083
(PANTING)

1639
01:51:59,964 --> 01:52:00,965
Is that her?

1640
01:52:01,257 --> 01:52:05,261
Red hair, IOI uniform,
doesn't know what planet she's on?

1641
01:52:05,344 --> 01:52:06,387
That's her.

1642
01:52:18,232 --> 01:52:20,943
I'm Toshiro. You know me as Daito.

1643
01:52:23,863 --> 01:52:24,906
ART3MIS: Oh.

1644
01:52:27,658 --> 01:52:29,076
Hey, Arty.

1645
01:52:31,120 --> 01:52:35,124
Yeah, I know.
Not what you were expecting, huh?

1646
01:52:35,291 --> 01:52:39,837
Yeah, I wasn't expecting
a late '30s-model postal van.

1647
01:52:41,923 --> 01:52:42,924
Wade?

1648
01:52:43,633 --> 01:52:45,885
Wait, I thought the Cataclyst went off.
How are you still playing?

1649
01:52:46,052 --> 01:52:48,554
Extra life, long story.
Sorry I shot you.

1650
01:52:50,890 --> 01:52:52,350
Sho?

1651
01:52:52,516 --> 01:52:54,894
What? Do I have to wear a sign saying,

1652
01:52:55,061 --> 01:52:58,022
"I am 11 years old, shoot me first"?
No, thanks.

1653
01:52:58,189 --> 01:53:00,358
- Dude, give me a hug.
- Ninjas don't hug!

1654
01:53:00,441 --> 01:53:01,943
All right, everybody,
hold on to somethin'.

1655
01:53:22,254 --> 01:53:23,506
(BEEPING)

1656
01:53:23,839 --> 01:53:25,132
Got you.

1657
01:53:28,886 --> 01:53:30,596
Come on, Nolan. Pick up.

1658
01:53:32,807 --> 01:53:35,351
F'Nale, tell me something good.

1659
01:53:35,643 --> 01:53:38,020
I've got a drone on their tail.
I'm close.

1660
01:53:38,187 --> 01:53:39,230
NOLAN: <i>Send me coordinates.</i>

1661
01:53:39,397 --> 01:53:41,607
Maybe you should
leave this to me, Nolan.

1662
01:53:41,691 --> 01:53:42,858
(LINE DISCONNECTS)

1663
01:53:43,484 --> 01:53:46,070
Nolan? Nolan.

1664
01:53:47,530 --> 01:53:48,656
Out.

1665
01:53:57,623 --> 01:54:00,084
Give me that.

1666
01:54:01,919 --> 01:54:03,462
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

1667
01:54:03,796 --> 01:54:05,506
AECH: What's goin' on out there?

1668
01:54:09,885 --> 01:54:12,346
SHO: The game is over for them.
What are they watching?

1669
01:54:14,849 --> 01:54:17,143
The final key! It's being broadcast.

1670
01:54:19,228 --> 01:54:20,730
WADE: <i>You see,</i>

1671
01:54:20,896 --> 01:54:23,441
<i>Warren Robinett was proud</i> of Adventure.

1672
01:54:23,607 --> 01:54:25,818
<i>He wanted people to know
who was behind it.</i>

1673
01:54:26,694 --> 01:54:29,238
That's why he created
the first digital Easter egg

1674
01:54:29,405 --> 01:54:31,949
and to find it,
you didn't even have to win.

1675
01:54:32,116 --> 01:54:36,120
You just had to blindly play,
searching around

1676
01:54:36,287 --> 01:54:39,373
in rooms for an invisible dot.

1677
01:54:40,416 --> 01:54:42,835
You took the dot back to the main screen

1678
01:54:43,002 --> 01:54:47,465
and that's when you found the first
Easter egg ever put in a video game.

1679
01:54:47,631 --> 01:54:48,883
- The creator's name.
- (BEEPING)

1680
01:55:13,574 --> 01:55:15,367
What's going on, man? I can't see shit.

1681
01:55:15,659 --> 01:55:17,036
Parzival just got the Crystal Key!

1682
01:55:20,414 --> 01:55:21,749
(ALL GRUNTING)

1683
01:55:32,343 --> 01:55:34,053
Do you want it or not?

1684
01:55:37,389 --> 01:55:39,183
Aech, what the hell's going on?

1685
01:55:39,475 --> 01:55:41,310
Just practicing my <i>Mario Kart.</i>
What do you think?

1686
01:55:41,477 --> 01:55:43,521
IOI's trying to kill us, man!

1687
01:55:57,785 --> 01:55:59,954
Everyone watching,
if you're in the Columbus stacks,

1688
01:56:00,121 --> 01:56:01,413
this is Parzival.

1689
01:56:01,580 --> 01:56:04,208
My real-world name is Wade Watts,
and we're gonna need your help.

1690
01:56:04,375 --> 01:56:05,793
Aech, head for the stacks!

1691
01:56:05,960 --> 01:56:07,586
Okay, hold on!

1692
01:56:08,212 --> 01:56:09,713
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1693
01:56:32,862 --> 01:56:34,822
Stick the key in, how hard is it?

1694
01:56:40,536 --> 01:56:41,704
Come on.

1695
01:56:49,170 --> 01:56:51,172
- (ALL CHEERING)
- Yeah! Yes!

1696
01:57:07,396 --> 01:57:08,606
That's it?

1697
01:57:09,440 --> 01:57:10,482
Yeah, that's it.

1698
01:57:10,649 --> 01:57:15,654
Now, you just sign these papers,
and the OASIS is yours.

1699
01:57:15,821 --> 01:57:19,950
You will be its sole proprietor.

1700
01:57:20,117 --> 01:57:21,577
That ain't so bad, is it?

1701
01:57:22,203 --> 01:57:24,038
(PANTING)

1702
01:57:29,376 --> 01:57:30,461
(YELLS)

1703
01:57:36,675 --> 01:57:38,135
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1704
01:57:43,432 --> 01:57:44,475
I'm gonna need a second.

1705
01:57:45,935 --> 01:57:46,936
(YELLS)

1706
01:57:53,525 --> 01:57:54,568
(GROANS)

1707
01:57:57,988 --> 01:57:59,073
(YELPS)

1708
01:58:13,170 --> 01:58:15,172
This is wrong.

1709
01:58:15,798 --> 01:58:18,676
This pen, this contract.

1710
01:58:21,929 --> 01:58:23,514
This is the moment
that Halliday made Morrow

1711
01:58:23,681 --> 01:58:25,557
sign over his shares in Gregarious.

1712
01:58:26,267 --> 01:58:28,352
That was the biggest mistake
of his life.

1713
01:58:28,936 --> 01:58:31,063
He knew that.

1714
01:58:32,815 --> 01:58:34,858
This can't be the end.

1715
01:58:36,068 --> 01:58:37,778
It's a test.

1716
01:58:42,324 --> 01:58:44,994
I won't make the same mistake you did.

1717
01:58:50,708 --> 01:58:52,584
Oh, good.

1718
01:58:55,296 --> 01:58:58,716
I just needed to be sure.

1719
01:59:12,730 --> 01:59:14,940
This is where you grew up.

1720
01:59:19,903 --> 01:59:21,363
(VIDEO GAME MUSIC)

1721
01:59:24,199 --> 01:59:26,577
Oh, that's just me a long time ago.

1722
01:59:27,161 --> 01:59:29,872
I like to have him around
from time to time.

1723
01:59:30,748 --> 01:59:32,374
Hey, I have to show you something.

1724
01:59:33,042 --> 01:59:34,585
This... Come on.

1725
01:59:34,752 --> 01:59:36,420
This is the button.

1726
01:59:36,587 --> 01:59:39,715
If you push it,
the whole simulation shuts down

1727
01:59:39,882 --> 01:59:43,344
and a tapeworm program will erase
all of the backup servers.

1728
01:59:43,510 --> 01:59:46,764
So you now have the power
to turn the OASIS off forever.

1729
01:59:47,264 --> 01:59:48,849
Do you understand?

1730
01:59:50,225 --> 01:59:51,352
(GRUNTS)

1731
01:59:52,269 --> 01:59:53,604
(PANTING)

1732
01:59:54,271 --> 01:59:55,272
Yeah,

1733
01:59:55,439 --> 01:59:57,232
try not to accidentally erase

1734
01:59:57,399 --> 02:00:00,069
the whole of the OASIS
on your first day.

1735
02:00:09,453 --> 02:00:11,163
The stacks are straight ahead!

1736
02:00:22,883 --> 02:00:24,134
(ALL GROANING)

1737
02:00:26,970 --> 02:00:29,765
HALLIDAY: Well, I expect you have to go.
I know I do.

1738
02:00:29,932 --> 02:00:32,309
So, now is the time for you
to receive your prize

1739
02:00:32,476 --> 02:00:34,853
because you won all three keys.

1740
02:00:35,020 --> 02:00:39,024
Once you take this egg,
the game will be over.

1741
02:00:39,733 --> 02:00:42,778
The egg, the egg...

1742
02:00:50,244 --> 02:00:52,496
We know what you did here.

1743
02:00:52,663 --> 02:00:55,958
You turn around and
walk out of here while you still can.

1744
02:01:04,883 --> 02:01:06,427
- (GUN COCKS)
- (CROWD GASPS)

1745
02:01:08,595 --> 02:01:10,973
I created the OASIS

1746
02:01:11,140 --> 02:01:14,810
because I never felt at home
in the real world.

1747
02:01:15,894 --> 02:01:19,189
I just didn't know how to connect
with the people there.

1748
02:01:20,357 --> 02:01:23,235
I was afraid for all of my life.

1749
02:01:23,861 --> 02:01:26,613
Right up until the day
I knew my life was ending.

1750
02:01:32,244 --> 02:01:36,081
Now, that... That was when
I realized that,

1751
02:01:37,249 --> 02:01:42,337
as terrifying and painful
as reality can be,

1752
02:01:43,213 --> 02:01:47,217
it's also the only place

1753
02:01:48,886 --> 02:01:50,512
that you can get a decent meal.

1754
02:01:57,186 --> 02:01:58,687
Because

1755
02:02:00,439 --> 02:02:02,024
reality

1756
02:02:07,196 --> 02:02:08,697
is real.

1757
02:02:08,864 --> 02:02:10,574
You understand what I'm saying?

1758
02:02:12,409 --> 02:02:15,037
Yes. Yes, I do.

1759
02:02:24,838 --> 02:02:26,089
He did it.

1760
02:02:27,799 --> 02:02:29,259
He got the egg.

1761
02:02:30,093 --> 02:02:31,345
Hooray.

1762
02:02:32,513 --> 02:02:34,139
- No!
- No! Please!

1763
02:03:00,582 --> 02:03:02,167
(VEHICLES APPROACHING)

1764
02:03:02,834 --> 02:03:04,419
(SIRENS WAILING)

1765
02:03:07,714 --> 02:03:08,966
OFFICER: Hold it!

1766
02:03:11,051 --> 02:03:14,054
Drop the gun! Now! On the ground!

1767
02:03:14,805 --> 02:03:17,391
Turn around! Hands on your head.

1768
02:03:17,558 --> 02:03:19,101
Walk back towards me.

1769
02:03:34,825 --> 02:03:39,246
WADE: Mr. Halliday.
Something I don't understand.

1770
02:03:40,080 --> 02:03:42,791
You're not an avatar, are you?

1771
02:03:43,417 --> 02:03:45,043
No.

1772
02:03:46,587 --> 02:03:48,589
Is Halliday really dead?

1773
02:03:50,257 --> 02:03:51,842
Yes.

1774
02:03:57,598 --> 02:03:59,349
Then what are you?

1775
02:04:02,603 --> 02:04:04,563
Goodbye, Parzival.

1776
02:04:06,231 --> 02:04:07,316
Thanks.

1777
02:04:08,859 --> 02:04:11,069
Thanks for playing my game.

1778
02:04:40,098 --> 02:04:41,391
Wade?

1779
02:04:42,809 --> 02:04:44,561
- Ogden Morrow?
- Ogden Morrow?

1780
02:04:44,728 --> 02:04:46,355
You can call me "Og."

1781
02:04:46,521 --> 02:04:49,274
Now, there are some people out here
that would very much like to meet you.

1782
02:04:49,858 --> 02:04:52,527
Wow, this is incredible.

1783
02:04:53,111 --> 02:04:55,864
It's an honor to meet you, Og, but I...

1784
02:05:00,077 --> 02:05:01,745
There's something I need to do first.

1785
02:05:05,666 --> 02:05:07,417
I'm not like Halliday.

1786
02:05:11,171 --> 02:05:13,215
I'm taking the leap.

1787
02:05:29,690 --> 02:05:30,899
We're looking for Wade Watts.

1788
02:05:32,818 --> 02:05:34,903
We need you to make a statement
about the clip you sent in

1789
02:05:35,070 --> 02:05:36,988
of Nolan Sorrento's confession.

1790
02:05:37,280 --> 02:05:39,366
Uh, that was me.

1791
02:05:40,033 --> 02:05:42,577
What? I record everything
in my workshop.

1792
02:05:49,000 --> 02:05:50,877
Help me out of this.

1793
02:05:57,217 --> 02:05:58,510
Who are you guys?

1794
02:05:59,511 --> 02:06:03,807
The people you need right now, lawyers.
From Gregarious Games.

1795
02:06:06,643 --> 02:06:08,270
They want your signature, Wade.

1796
02:06:16,236 --> 02:06:18,321
I'm splitting it with my clan.

1797
02:06:18,488 --> 02:06:20,282
We're gonna run things together.

1798
02:06:24,828 --> 02:06:26,872
That's a good choice.

1799
02:06:27,038 --> 02:06:29,040
(CROWD CHEERING)

1800
02:06:54,816 --> 02:06:57,861
F'Nale, listen to me very carefully.

1801
02:06:58,445 --> 02:06:59,529
(NOLAN GROANS)

1802
02:07:07,078 --> 02:07:09,831
Mr. Morrow... I mean, Og,

1803
02:07:09,998 --> 02:07:11,291
how'd you get here so fast?

1804
02:07:11,458 --> 02:07:13,627
I flew from the stars
on my magic sleigh.

1805
02:07:14,211 --> 02:07:16,630
(CHUCKLES) Everyone's been watching.

1806
02:07:16,797 --> 02:07:20,008
Of course, I've been watching
a little closer than most.

1807
02:07:24,054 --> 02:07:25,472
You?

1808
02:07:25,972 --> 02:07:27,182
You're the Curator?

1809
02:07:30,936 --> 02:07:33,146
(IN BRITISH ACCENT)
Well played, Parzival.

1810
02:07:34,397 --> 02:07:36,274
(IN NORMAL VOICE)
Jim told me nothing about the contest,

1811
02:07:36,441 --> 02:07:39,653
so there was no rule
about me losing a bet to a smart kid.

1812
02:07:39,820 --> 02:07:41,488
Not that you needed my help.

1813
02:07:42,447 --> 02:07:46,409
You figured out that Kira was the key
on your own.

1814
02:07:46,785 --> 02:07:49,412
Yeah, but... Kira wasn't the key.

1815
02:07:50,747 --> 02:07:52,624
It was you, Mr. Morrow.

1816
02:07:54,751 --> 02:07:56,419
You were the Rosebud.

1817
02:07:56,586 --> 02:07:58,797
And Halliday's biggest regret was

1818
02:08:00,507 --> 02:08:02,092
losing his only friend.

1819
02:08:04,970 --> 02:08:06,263
(CLEARS THROAT)

1820
02:08:06,346 --> 02:08:08,515
You know, Jim used to say the OASIS

1821
02:08:08,682 --> 02:08:11,142
was never supposed to be
a one-player game.

1822
02:08:14,855 --> 02:08:17,482
Now, who do we have here?

1823
02:08:17,649 --> 02:08:20,151
Oh. Well, look who it is.

1824
02:08:20,318 --> 02:08:21,903
It's my heroes, the High Five.

1825
02:08:22,070 --> 02:08:23,572
- You must be Art3mis.
- Samantha.

1826
02:08:23,738 --> 02:08:25,532
WADE: <i>The High Five took over the OASIS,</i>

1827
02:08:25,699 --> 02:08:27,158
<i>and the first thing we did</i>

1828
02:08:27,325 --> 02:08:30,662
<i>was sign Ogden Morrow
to a non-exclusive consultancy.</i>

1829
02:08:30,829 --> 02:08:33,665
<i>The salary, per his demand,</i>

1830
02:08:33,832 --> 02:08:36,918
<i>was 25 cents. One quarter.</i>

1831
02:08:37,085 --> 02:08:38,295
(COIN CLINKS)

1832
02:08:40,297 --> 02:08:42,549
<i>With his guidance,
our second move was to ban</i>

1833
02:08:42,716 --> 02:08:45,385
<i>any loyalty centers
from accessing the OASIS.</i>

1834
02:08:46,177 --> 02:08:49,598
<i>IOI had no choice.
They shut 'em all down.</i>

1835
02:08:52,392 --> 02:08:54,853
<i>The third thing we did
wasn't as popular.</i>

1836
02:08:55,395 --> 02:08:58,523
<i>We closed the OASIS
on Tuesdays and Thursdays.</i>

1837
02:08:59,399 --> 02:09:01,735
<i>I know, it sounds like a weird move,</i>

1838
02:09:01,902 --> 02:09:04,779
<i>but people need to spend
more time in the real world.</i>

1839
02:09:06,448 --> 02:09:09,367
<i>'Cause, like Halliday said,</i>

1840
02:09:09,534 --> 02:09:13,872
<i>reality is the only thing that's real.</i>

1841
02:19:49,340 --> 02:19:50,341
English - SDH

